-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, sexual offences and offences of
-- selling, buying and importing persons for prostitution: the sections the
-- first pass left deferred, ss 372, 373, 373A, 376B to 376H, 377 and 377B.
-- Completion pass of 2026-11-04 by one Sonnet 5.5 agent.
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text),
-- registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt lines 8071-9050.
--
-- What a reader must know before reading:
--
-- * Each offence has the contract's four items: a facts record, a defining
--   predicate, `offence under s N` and `charge under s N`. The ladders are
--   BOOLEAN: FALSE there means "the elements are not made out on the facts
--   stated", not "the text says no". The definitions and rules of reading
--   in this module (subsections that say what a word means, what is
--   presumed, or what is immaterial) return MAYBE BOOLEAN or a named
--   constructor: JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words,
--   NOTHING (or a "not covered" constructor) everywhere else. Every such
--   branch is marked FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind in a comment, and
--   NOTES.md has "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".
-- * Where an offence is defined by another offence, the other offence's facts
--   are a field of this one (ss 376C and 376G(4)), supplied by the caller for
--   the same act.
-- * Where the section is "subject to" an Act that is not in the sources,
--   or uses a word that Act defines, the fact is an input (a leaf with a
--   @desc), never a guess.
-- * `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual` is the definition of "sexual" and is in
--   pc-body-b-deferred-images.l4, with the rest of s 377C.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-body-b-kidnapping`
IMPORT `pc-body-b-sexual`

§ `Chapter 16 - ss 372-377B, completed`


§§ `s 372 - selling minor for purposes of prostitution, etc.`

-- src:8071 | Selling minor for purposes of prostitution, etc.
-- src:8073 | 372. Whoever sells, lets to hire, or otherwise disposes of any person below 21 years
-- src:8074 | of age with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose
-- src:8075 | of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral
-- src:8076 | purpose, or knowing it to be likely that such person will at any age be employed or used
-- src:8077 | for any such purpose, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
-- src:8078 | to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
-- src:8080 | Explanation.—When a female below 21 years of age is sold, let for hire, or otherwise disposed of to
-- src:8081 | a prostitute or to any person who keeps or manages a brothel, the person so disposing of such female
-- src:8082 | shall, until the contrary is proved, be presumed to have disposed of her with the intent that she shall be
-- src:8083 | used for the purpose of prostitution.
-- The Explanation's presumption is a function of its own, below: it is a rebuttable presumption of intent,
-- not an element, so the ladder reads the intent and the knowledge as the caller states them (FORK DEF-B1).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 372 (src:8071-8083)
DECLARE `Selling Minor Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person sold, let to hire or disposed of, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by selling the said minor to the keeper of a brothel"
    `the accused sells, lets to hire, or otherwise disposes of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused sell, let to hire, or otherwise dispose of a person?
    `the person is below 21 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person below 21 years of age? Set from the helper `below 21 years of age` on the person's age
    `the accused intends that the person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend that the person should, at any age, be employed or used for prostitution, for illicit intercourse with any person, or for any unlawful and immoral purpose? The Explanation presumes this intent for a female below 21 disposed of to a prostitute or brothel-keeper: see `s 372 Explanation the intent that she shall be used for prostitution`
    `the accused knows it to be likely that the person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it to be likely that the person would, at any age, be employed or used for any such purpose?

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 372 (src:8073-8078)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 372 of the Penal Code 1871 (selling a person below 21 years of age for prostitution or another unlawful and immoral purpose)
GIVEN f IS A `Selling Minor Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sells a person below 21 years of age within section 372` f IF
        "Whoever sells, lets to hire, or otherwise disposes of any person below 21 years of age"
   ...  (f's `the accused sells, lets to hire, or otherwise disposes of a person` AND f's `the person is below 21 years of age`)
   ...  "with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose, or knowing it to be likely that such person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose"
   ...    (f's `the accused intends that the person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose` OR f's `the accused knows it to be likely that the person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 372 (src:8073-8078)
`punishment prescribed by s 372` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "372"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 372 (src:8073-8078)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 372 of the Penal Code 1871 (selling minor for purposes of prostitution, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Selling Minor Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 372` f IF
        "shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
   ...  `sells a person below 21 years of age within section 372` f

GIVEN f IS A `Selling Minor Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of selling minor for purposes of prostitution, etc. not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused sells, lets to hire, or otherwise disposes of a person` AND f's `the person is below 21 years of age`) "the accused sells, lets to hire, or otherwise disposes of a person below 21 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused intends that the person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose` OR f's `the accused knows it to be likely that the person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose`) "the accused intends that the person be employed or used for prostitution, illicit intercourse or an unlawful and immoral purpose, or knows it to be likely"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 372` f) "the elements of section 372 taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 372 (src:8073-8078)
@export Frame a charge under section 372 of the Penal Code 1871 (selling minor for purposes of prostitution, etc.), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Selling Minor Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 372` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "372" "selling minor for purposes of prostitution, etc."
        (`punishment prescribed by s 372`'s words)
        (`offence under s 372` f)
        (CONCAT "did sell, let to hire or otherwise dispose of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 21 years of age, ", (IF f's `the accused intends that the person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose` THEN "with intent that the said person should be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse or for an unlawful and immoral purpose" ELSE "knowing it to be likely that the said person would be employed or used for such a purpose"), ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of selling minor for purposes of prostitution, etc. not made out` f)

-- 372 Explanation: "When a female below 21 years of age is sold, let for hire,
-- or otherwise disposed of to a prostitute or to any person who keeps or
-- manages a brothel, the person so disposing of such female shall, until the
-- contrary is proved, be presumed to have disposed of her with the intent that
-- she shall be used for the purpose of prostitution."
-- 373 Explanation is the mirror: a prostitute or brothel-keeper who obtains a
-- female below 21.
DECLARE `Presumption of intent to use for prostitution` IS ONE OF
    `presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have had the intent that she shall be used for the purpose of prostitution`
    `not covered by this Explanation`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 372 Explanation (src:8080-8083)
@export What the Explanation to section 372 of the Penal Code 1871 presumes: that a person who disposes of a female below 21 years of age to a prostitute or a brothel-keeper intended her to be used for prostitution, until the contrary is proved
GIVEN `the person disposed of is a female below 21 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who was sold, let for hire or otherwise disposed of a female below 21 years of age?
      `the disposal is to a prostitute or to any person who keeps or manages a brothel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was she disposed of to a prostitute, or to any person who keeps or manages a brothel?
GIVETH A `Presumption of intent to use for prostitution`
`s 372 Explanation the intent that she shall be used for prostitution` MEANS
    IF `the person disposed of is a female below 21 years of age` AND `the disposal is to a prostitute or to any person who keeps or manages a brothel`
    THEN `presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have had the intent that she shall be used for the purpose of prostitution`
    ELSE `not covered by this Explanation`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Explanation presumes the intent only for a female below 21 disposed of to a prostitute or brothel-keeper; it does not say that the intent is not to be found in any other case



§§ `s 373 - buying minor for purposes of prostitution, etc.`

-- src:8085 | Buying minor for purposes of prostitution, etc.
-- src:8087 | 373. Whoever buys, hires or otherwise obtains possession of any person below
-- src:8088 | 21 years of age with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the
-- src:8089 | purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and
-- src:8090 | immoral purpose, or knowing it to be likely that such person will at any age be employed
-- src:8091 | or used for any such purpose, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- src:8092 | extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
-- src:8094 | Explanation.—Any prostitute, or any person keeping or managing a brothel, who buys, hires or
-- src:8095 | otherwise obtains possession of a female below 21 years of age shall, until the contrary is proved, be
-- src:8096 | presumed to have obtained possession of such female with the intent that she shall be used for the
-- src:8097 | purpose of prostitution.
-- The Explanation's presumption is a function of its own, below (FORK DEF-B1).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373 (src:8085-8097)
DECLARE `Buying Minor Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person bought, hired or obtained, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by buying the said minor from her guardian"
    `the accused buys, hires or otherwise obtains possession of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused buy, hire or otherwise obtain possession of a person?
    `the person is below 21 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person below 21 years of age? Set from the helper `below 21 years of age` on the person's age
    `the accused intends that the person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend that the person should, at any age, be employed or used for prostitution, for illicit intercourse with any person, or for any unlawful and immoral purpose? The Explanation presumes this intent for a prostitute or brothel-keeper who obtains a female below 21: see `s 373 Explanation the intent that she shall be used for prostitution`
    `the accused knows it to be likely that the person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it to be likely that the person would, at any age, be employed or used for any such purpose?

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373 (src:8087-8092)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 373 of the Penal Code 1871 (buying a person below 21 years of age for prostitution or another unlawful and immoral purpose)
GIVEN f IS A `Buying Minor Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `buys a person below 21 years of age within section 373` f IF
        "Whoever buys, hires or otherwise obtains possession of any person below 21 years of age"
   ...  (f's `the accused buys, hires or otherwise obtains possession of a person` AND f's `the person is below 21 years of age`)
   ...  "with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose, or knowing it to be likely that such person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose"
   ...    (f's `the accused intends that the person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose` OR f's `the accused knows it to be likely that the person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373 (src:8087-8092)
`punishment prescribed by s 373` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "373"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373 (src:8087-8092)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 373 of the Penal Code 1871 (buying minor for purposes of prostitution, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Buying Minor Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 373` f IF
        "shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
   ...  `buys a person below 21 years of age within section 373` f

GIVEN f IS A `Buying Minor Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of buying minor for purposes of prostitution, etc. not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused buys, hires or otherwise obtains possession of a person` AND f's `the person is below 21 years of age`) "the accused buys, hires or otherwise obtains possession of a person below 21 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused intends that the person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose` OR f's `the accused knows it to be likely that the person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose`) "the accused intends that the person be employed or used for prostitution, illicit intercourse or an unlawful and immoral purpose, or knows it to be likely"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 373` f) "the elements of section 373 taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373 (src:8087-8092)
@export Frame a charge under section 373 of the Penal Code 1871 (buying minor for purposes of prostitution, etc.), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Buying Minor Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 373` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "373" "buying minor for purposes of prostitution, etc."
        (`punishment prescribed by s 373`'s words)
        (`offence under s 373` f)
        (CONCAT "did buy, hire or otherwise obtain possession of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 21 years of age, ", (IF f's `the accused intends that the person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose` THEN "with intent that the said person should be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse or for an unlawful and immoral purpose" ELSE "knowing it to be likely that the said person would be employed or used for such a purpose"), ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of buying minor for purposes of prostitution, etc. not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373 Explanation (src:8094-8097)
@export What the Explanation to section 373 of the Penal Code 1871 presumes: that a prostitute or brothel-keeper who obtains a female below 21 years of age intended her to be used for prostitution, until the contrary is proved
GIVEN `the person who obtains possession is a prostitute or a person keeping or managing a brothel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who bought, hired or otherwise obtained possession a prostitute, or a person who keeps or manages a brothel?
      `the person obtained is a female below 21 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person obtained a female below 21 years of age?
GIVETH A `Presumption of intent to use for prostitution`
`s 373 Explanation the intent that she shall be used for prostitution` MEANS
    IF `the person who obtains possession is a prostitute or a person keeping or managing a brothel` AND `the person obtained is a female below 21 years of age`
    THEN `presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have had the intent that she shall be used for the purpose of prostitution`
    ELSE `not covered by this Explanation`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Explanation presumes the intent only for a prostitute or brothel-keeper who obtains a female below 21; it does not say that the intent is not to be found in any other case



§§ `s 373A - importing woman for purposes of prostitution, etc.`

-- src:8099 | Importing woman for purposes of prostitution, etc.
-- src:8101 | 373A. Whoever —
-- src:8103 | (a) by any false pretence, false representation, or fraudulent or deceitful
-- src:8104 | means, brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore any woman with intent
-- src:8105 | that such woman may be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution;
-- src:8107 | (b) brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore any woman with intent that
-- src:8108 | such woman may be sold or bought for the purpose of prostitution; or
-- src:8110 | (c) sells or buys any woman for the purpose of prostitution,
-- src:8112 | shall be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years, and shall also be
-- src:8113 | liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373A (src:8099-8113)
DECLARE `Importing Woman Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the woman brought into Singapore, sold or bought, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by bringing the said woman from Jakarta on a promise of work as a cook"
    `the accused by any false pretence, false representation, or fraudulent or deceitful means brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused, by any false pretence, false representation, or fraudulent or deceitful means, bring a woman into Singapore, or assist in bringing her? (s 373A(a))
    `the accused intends that the woman may be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend that the woman might be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution? (s 373A(a))
    `the accused brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused bring a woman into Singapore, or assist in bringing her, by whatever means? (s 373A(b))
    `the accused intends that the woman may be sold or bought for the purpose of prostitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend that the woman might be sold or bought for the purpose of prostitution? (s 373A(b))
    `the accused sells or buys a woman for the purpose of prostitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused sell or buy a woman for the purpose of prostitution? (s 373A(c))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373A (src:8101-8110)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 373A of the Penal Code 1871 (bringing a woman into Singapore for prostitution by deceit, bringing her for sale or purchase for prostitution, or selling or buying her for prostitution)
GIVEN f IS A `Importing Woman Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imports, sells or buys a woman for prostitution within section 373A` f IF
        "Whoever (a) by any false pretence, false representation, or fraudulent or deceitful means, brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore any woman with intent that such woman may be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution; (b) brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore any woman with intent that such woman may be sold or bought for the purpose of prostitution; or (c) sells or buys any woman for the purpose of prostitution"
   ...    ((f's `the accused by any false pretence, false representation, or fraudulent or deceitful means brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore a woman` AND f's `the accused intends that the woman may be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution`) OR (f's `the accused brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore a woman` AND f's `the accused intends that the woman may be sold or bought for the purpose of prostitution`) OR f's `the accused sells or buys a woman for the purpose of prostitution`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373A (src:8112-8113)
`punishment prescribed by s 373A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "373A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373A (src:8101-8113)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 373A of the Penal Code 1871 (importing woman for purposes of prostitution, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Importing Woman Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 373A` f IF
        "shall be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
   ...  `imports, sells or buys a woman for prostitution within section 373A` f

GIVEN f IS A `Importing Woman Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of importing woman for purposes of prostitution, etc. not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` ((f's `the accused by any false pretence, false representation, or fraudulent or deceitful means brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore a woman` AND f's `the accused intends that the woman may be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution`) OR (f's `the accused brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore a woman` AND f's `the accused intends that the woman may be sold or bought for the purpose of prostitution`) OR f's `the accused sells or buys a woman for the purpose of prostitution`) "the accused, by deceit, brings a woman into Singapore for prostitution; or brings her into Singapore for sale or purchase for prostitution; or sells or buys her for prostitution"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 373A` f) "the elements of section 373A taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 373A (src:8101-8113)
@export Frame a charge under section 373A of the Penal Code 1871 (importing woman for purposes of prostitution, etc.), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Importing Woman Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 373A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "373A" "importing woman for purposes of prostitution, etc."
        (`punishment prescribed by s 373A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 373A` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `the accused sells or buys a woman for the purpose of prostitution` THEN "did sell or buy " ELSE "did bring, or assist in bringing, into Singapore "), (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), (IF f's `the accused sells or buys a woman for the purpose of prostitution` THEN ", a woman, for the purpose of prostitution" ELSE (IF f's `the accused by any false pretence, false representation, or fraudulent or deceitful means brings, or assists in bringing, into Singapore a woman` THEN ", a woman, by false pretence, false representation or fraudulent or deceitful means, with intent that she be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution" ELSE ", a woman, with intent that she be sold or bought for the purpose of prostitution")), ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of importing woman for purposes of prostitution, etc. not made out` f)


§§ `s 376B - commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age`

-- src:8359 | Commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age
-- src:8361 | 376B.—(1) Any person who obtains for consideration the sexual services of a person,
-- src:8362 | who is below 18 years of age, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
-- src:8363 | may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- src:8365 | (2) Any person who communicates with another person for the purpose of obtaining
-- src:8366 | for consideration, the sexual services of a person who is below 18 years of age, shall be
-- src:8367 | punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or
-- src:8368 | with both.
-- src:8370 | (3) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for any sexual services
-- src:8371 | obtained from that person’s spouse.
-- src:8373 | (4) In this section, “sexual services” means any sexual services involving —
-- src:8375 | (a) sexual penetration of the vagina or anus, as the case may be, of a person by
-- src:8376 | a part of another person’s body (other than the penis) or by anything else;
-- src:8378 | (b) penetration of the vagina, anus or mouth, as the case may be, of a person
-- src:8381 | by a man’s penis; or
-- src:8383 | (c) touching which is sexual of another person or of himself or herself.
-- Subsection (4) defines "sexual services" (a closed list, "means"): `s 376B(4) the services are sexual services`, below.
-- Subsection (3) bars both offences for services obtained from the accused's spouse ("an offence under this section").
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B (src:8359-8383)
DECLARE `Commercial Sex Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person whose sexual services were obtained or sought, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by paying the said minor $200 for sexual intercourse"
    `the accused obtains for consideration the sexual services of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obtain, for consideration, the sexual services of a person? (s 376B(1))
    `the accused communicates with another person for the purpose of obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused communicate with another person for the purpose of obtaining, for consideration, the sexual services of a person? (s 376B(2))
    `the person whose sexual services are in question is below 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person whose sexual services were obtained or sought below 18 years of age? Set from the helper `below 18 years of age` on that person's age
    `the services are sexual services within section 376B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the services "sexual services" as s 376B(4) gives the meaning - involving sexual penetration of the vagina or anus by a part of another person's body (other than the penis) or by anything else, penetration of the vagina, anus or mouth by a man's penis, or touching which is sexual? Set from `s 376B(4) the services are sexual services`
    `the sexual services were obtained from the accused's spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the sexual services obtained from the accused's own spouse? (s 376B(3): then there is no offence under the section)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B (src:8361-8363)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376B(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obtains the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age within section 376B(1)` f IF
        "Any person who obtains for consideration the sexual services of a person, who is below 18 years of age"
   ...  (f's `the accused obtains for consideration the sexual services of a person` AND f's `the services are sexual services within section 376B(4)` AND f's `the person whose sexual services are in question is below 18 years of age`)
   ...  "(3) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for any sexual services obtained from that person's spouse"
   ...  (NOT (f's `the sexual services were obtained from the accused's spouse`))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for any sexual services obtained from that person's spouse"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B (src:8365-8368)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376B(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (communicating for the purpose of obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `communicates to obtain the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age within section 376B(2)` f IF
        "Any person who communicates with another person for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person who is below 18 years of age"
   ...  (f's `the accused communicates with another person for the purpose of obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person` AND f's `the services are sexual services within section 376B(4)` AND f's `the person whose sexual services are in question is below 18 years of age`)
   ...  "(3) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for any sexual services obtained from that person's spouse"
   ...  (NOT (f's `the sexual services were obtained from the accused's spouse`))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for any sexual services obtained from that person's spouse"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B(1) (src:8361-8363)
`punishment prescribed by s 376B(1)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376B(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B(1) (src:8361-8363)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376B(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (commercial sex with a minor below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376B(1)` f IF
        "shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
   ...  `obtains the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age within section 376B(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused obtains for consideration the sexual services of a person` AND f's `the services are sexual services within section 376B(4)` AND f's `the person whose sexual services are in question is below 18 years of age`) "the accused obtains for consideration the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `the sexual services were obtained from the accused's spouse`)) "the sexual services were not obtained from the accused's spouse (section 376B(3))"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376B(1)` f) "the elements of section 376B(1) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B(1) (src:8361-8363)
@export Frame a charge under section 376B(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (commercial sex with a minor below 18 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376B(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376B(1)" "commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376B(1)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376B(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "did obtain for consideration the sexual services of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 18 years of age, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B(2) (src:8365-8368)
`punishment prescribed by s 376B(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376B(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B(2) (src:8365-8368)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376B(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (communicating to obtain commercial sex with a minor below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376B(2)` f IF
        "shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
   ...  `communicates to obtain the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age within section 376B(2)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of communicating to obtain commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused communicates with another person for the purpose of obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person` AND f's `the services are sexual services within section 376B(4)` AND f's `the person whose sexual services are in question is below 18 years of age`) "the accused communicates with another person for the purpose of obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `the sexual services were obtained from the accused's spouse`)) "the sexual services were not obtained from the accused's spouse (section 376B(3))"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376B(2)` f) "the elements of section 376B(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B(2) (src:8365-8368)
@export Frame a charge under section 376B(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (communicating to obtain commercial sex with a minor below 18 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376B(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376B(2)" "communicating to obtain commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376B(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376B(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did communicate with another person for the purpose of obtaining for consideration the sexual services of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 18 years of age, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of communicating to obtain commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age not made out` f)

-- 376B(4): "sexual services" means any sexual services involving (a)-(c)
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376B(4) (src:8373-8383)
@export Whether services are "sexual services" within section 376B(4) of the Penal Code 1871: services involving sexual penetration of the vagina or anus by a part of another person's body (other than the penis) or by anything else, penetration of the vagina, anus or mouth by a man's penis, or touching which is sexual
GIVEN `the services involve sexual penetration of the vagina or anus of a person by a part of another person's body (other than the penis) or by anything else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the services involve that?
      `the services involve penetration of the vagina, anus or mouth of a person by a man's penis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the services involve that?
      `the services involve touching which is sexual of another person or of himself or herself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the services involve touching which is sexual? "Sexual" is read with `s 377C(2) the touching is sexual`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376B(4) the services are sexual services` MEANS
    IF `the services involve sexual penetration of the vagina or anus of a person by a part of another person's body (other than the penis) or by anything else`
        OR `the services involve penetration of the vagina, anus or mouth of a person by a man's penis`
        OR `the services involve touching which is sexual of another person or of himself or herself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"sexual services\" means any sexual services involving ..." (a closed list)



§§ `s 376C - commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age outside Singapore`

-- src:8387 | Commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age outside Singapore
-- src:8389 | 376C.—(1) Any person, being a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, who
-- src:8390 | does, outside Singapore, any act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence
-- src:8391 | under section 376B, shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:8393 | (1A) To avoid doubt, any person (A) who does in Singapore, any act involving a
-- src:8394 | person below 18 years of age (B) who is outside Singapore, that would if B were in
-- src:8395 | Singapore constitute an offence under section 376B, shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:8399 | (1B) Any person who does outside Singapore, any act involving a person below
-- src:8400 | 18 years of age who is in Singapore, that would if done in Singapore constitute an
-- src:8401 | offence under section 376B, shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:8405 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with the
-- src:8406 | same punishment with which he would have been punished had he been convicted of an
-- src:8407 | offence under section 376B.
-- The act "that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B" is read over a nested
-- `Commercial Sex Facts` for the same act, which the caller supplies (FORK DEF-B2). The punishment is borrowed from s 376B (subsection (2)):
-- the charge states the words of s 376B(1) or s 376B(2), whichever offence the nested facts make out.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376C (src:8387-8407)
DECLARE `Commercial Sex Abroad Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person below 18 years of age involved in the act, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by paying the said minor in Batam for sexual intercourse"
    `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore? (s 376C(1))
    `the accused does the act outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do the act outside Singapore? (s 376C(1), (1B))
    `the accused does the act in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do the act in Singapore? (s 376C(1A))
    `the act involves a person below 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act involve a person below 18 years of age? (s 376C(1A), (1B))
    `the person below 18 years of age is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person outside Singapore? (s 376C(1A))
    `the person below 18 years of age is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person in Singapore? (s 376C(1B))
    `the act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B` IS A `Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the same act, read as if it were done in Singapore (or, in s 376C(1A), as if B were in Singapore): would they constitute an offence under s 376B? Supply them as `Commercial Sex Facts`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376C (src:8389-8401)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376C of the Penal Code 1871 (an act that would constitute an offence under section 376B, done outside Singapore by a citizen or permanent resident; done in Singapore involving a minor who is outside it; or done outside Singapore involving a minor who is in it)
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Abroad Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `does an act that would be an offence under section 376B within section 376C` f IF
        "(1) Any person, being a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, who does, outside Singapore, any act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B; (1A) any person (A) who does in Singapore, any act involving a person below 18 years of age (B) who is outside Singapore, that would if B were in Singapore constitute an offence under section 376B; (1B) any person who does outside Singapore, any act involving a person below 18 years of age who is in Singapore, that would if done in Singapore constitute an offence under section 376B, shall be guilty of an offence"
   ...    ((f's `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore` AND f's `the accused does the act outside Singapore`) OR (f's `the accused does the act in Singapore` AND f's `the act involves a person below 18 years of age` AND f's `the person below 18 years of age is outside Singapore`) OR (f's `the accused does the act outside Singapore` AND f's `the act involves a person below 18 years of age` AND f's `the person below 18 years of age is in Singapore`))
   ...    ((`offence under s 376B(1)` (f's `the act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B`)) OR (`offence under s 376B(2)` (f's `the act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B`)))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376C(2) (src:8405-8407)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376C(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (commercial sex with a minor below 18 years of age, outside Singapore)
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Abroad Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376C(2)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with the same punishment with which he would have been punished had he been convicted of an offence under section 376B"
   ...  `does an act that would be an offence under section 376B within section 376C` f

GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Abroad Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age outside Singapore not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` ((f's `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore` AND f's `the accused does the act outside Singapore`) OR (f's `the accused does the act in Singapore` AND f's `the act involves a person below 18 years of age` AND f's `the person below 18 years of age is outside Singapore`) OR (f's `the accused does the act outside Singapore` AND f's `the act involves a person below 18 years of age` AND f's `the person below 18 years of age is in Singapore`)) "the accused is a citizen or permanent resident who acts outside Singapore; or acts in Singapore involving a person below 18 who is outside Singapore; or acts outside Singapore involving a person below 18 who is in Singapore"),
        (`missing unless` ((`offence under s 376B(1)` (f's `the act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B`)) OR (`offence under s 376B(2)` (f's `the act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B`))) "the act would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376C(2)` f) "the elements of section 376C(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376C(2) (src:8405-8407)
@export Frame a charge under section 376C(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (commercial sex with a minor below 18 years of age, outside Singapore), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Commercial Sex Abroad Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376C(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376C(2)" "commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age outside Singapore"
        (IF (`offence under s 376B(1)` (f's `the act that would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B`)) THEN `punishment prescribed by s 376B(1)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 376B(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376C(2)` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore` THEN "being a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore, did outside Singapore an act, to wit, " ELSE (IF f's `the accused does the act in Singapore` THEN "did in Singapore an act involving " ELSE "did outside Singapore an act involving ")), (IF f's `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore` THEN "" ELSE CONCAT (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 18 years of age, "), "which would, if done in Singapore, constitute an offence under section 376B of the Penal Code 1871, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age outside Singapore not made out` f)


§§ `s 376D - tour outside Singapore for commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age`

-- src:8411 | Tour outside Singapore for commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age
-- src:8413 | 376D.—(1) Any person who —
-- src:8415 | (a) makes or organises any travel arrangements for or on behalf of any other
-- src:8416 | person with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other
-- src:8417 | person of an offence under section 376C, whether or not such an offence is
-- src:8418 | actually committed by that other person;
-- src:8420 | (b) transports any other person to a place outside Singapore with the intention
-- src:8421 | of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under
-- src:8422 | section 376C, whether or not such an offence is actually committed by that
-- src:8423 | other person; or
-- src:8425 | (c) prints, publishes or distributes any information that is intended to promote
-- src:8426 | conduct that would constitute an offence under section 376C, or to assist
-- src:8427 | any other person to engage in such conduct,
-- src:8429 | shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:8431 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(c), the publication of information means
-- src:8434 | publication of information by any means, whether by written, electronic, or other form of
-- src:8435 | communication.
-- src:8437 | (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with
-- src:8438 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- Whether the offence under s 376C is "actually committed by that other person" is immaterial: the ladder has no leaf for it.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376D (src:8411-8438)
DECLARE `Travel for Commercial Sex Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the other person for whom the arrangements were made or whom the accused transported (leave blank for information published to the public)
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by booking flights and a hotel in Phnom Penh for the said person"
    `the accused makes or organises travel arrangements for or on behalf of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make or organise travel arrangements for or on behalf of any other person? (s 376D(1)(a))
    `the accused makes or organises the travel arrangements with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under section 376C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do so with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under s 376C, whether or not it is actually committed? (s 376D(1)(a))
    `the accused transports any other person to a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused transport any other person to a place outside Singapore? (s 376D(1)(b))
    `the accused transports that person with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under section 376C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do so with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under s 376C, whether or not it is actually committed? (s 376D(1)(b))
    `the accused prints, publishes or distributes information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused print, publish or distribute information? Publication is by any means, whether written, electronic or other form of communication (s 376D(2); see `s 376D(2) the means of publication`) (s 376D(1)(c))
    `the information is intended to promote conduct that would constitute an offence under section 376C, or to assist any other person to engage in such conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information intended to promote conduct that would constitute an offence under s 376C, or to assist any other person to engage in such conduct? (s 376D(1)(c))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376D (src:8413-8429)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376D(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (making travel arrangements for, transporting, or publishing information to promote, an offence under section 376C)
GIVEN f IS A `Travel for Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `organises a tour for commercial sex with a minor within section 376D` f IF
        "Any person who (a) makes or organises any travel arrangements for or on behalf of any other person with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under section 376C, whether or not such an offence is actually committed by that other person; (b) transports any other person to a place outside Singapore with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under section 376C; or (c) prints, publishes or distributes any information that is intended to promote conduct that would constitute an offence under section 376C, or to assist any other person to engage in such conduct, shall be guilty of an offence"
   ...    ((f's `the accused makes or organises travel arrangements for or on behalf of any other person` AND f's `the accused makes or organises the travel arrangements with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under section 376C`) OR (f's `the accused transports any other person to a place outside Singapore` AND f's `the accused transports that person with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under section 376C`) OR (f's `the accused prints, publishes or distributes information` AND f's `the information is intended to promote conduct that would constitute an offence under section 376C, or to assist any other person to engage in such conduct`))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376D(3) (src:8437-8438)
`punishment prescribed by s 376D(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376D(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376D(3) (src:8437-8438)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376D(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (tour outside Singapore for commercial sex with a minor below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Travel for Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376D(3)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
   ...  `organises a tour for commercial sex with a minor within section 376D` f

GIVEN f IS A `Travel for Commercial Sex Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of tour outside Singapore for commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` ((f's `the accused makes or organises travel arrangements for or on behalf of any other person` AND f's `the accused makes or organises the travel arrangements with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under section 376C`) OR (f's `the accused transports any other person to a place outside Singapore` AND f's `the accused transports that person with the intention of facilitating the commission by that other person of an offence under section 376C`) OR (f's `the accused prints, publishes or distributes information` AND f's `the information is intended to promote conduct that would constitute an offence under section 376C, or to assist any other person to engage in such conduct`)) "the accused makes or organises travel arrangements with the intention of facilitating an offence under section 376C; or transports a person outside Singapore with that intention; or prints, publishes or distributes information intended to promote conduct that would constitute an offence under section 376C, or to assist another person to engage in it"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376D(3)` f) "the elements of section 376D(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376D(3) (src:8437-8438)
@export Frame a charge under section 376D(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (tour outside Singapore for commercial sex with a minor below 18 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Travel for Commercial Sex Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376D(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376D(3)" "tour outside Singapore for commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376D(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376D(3)` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `the accused makes or organises travel arrangements for or on behalf of any other person` THEN CONCAT "did make or organise travel arrangements for or on behalf of ", (f's victim), " with the intention of facilitating the commission by that person of an offence under section 376C of the Penal Code 1871" ELSE (IF f's `the accused transports any other person to a place outside Singapore` THEN CONCAT "did transport ", (f's victim), " to a place outside Singapore with the intention of facilitating the commission by that person of an offence under section 376C of the Penal Code 1871" ELSE "did print, publish or distribute information intended to promote conduct that would constitute an offence under section 376C of the Penal Code 1871, or to assist another person to engage in such conduct")), ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of tour outside Singapore for commercial sex with minor below 18 years of age not made out` f)

-- 376D(2): the publication of information means publication by any means
DECLARE `Form of communication` IS ONE OF
    written
    electronic
    `some other form of communication`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376D(2) (src:8431-8435)
@export Whether a form of communication is "publication of information" within section 376D(2) of the Penal Code 1871: "publication of information by any means, whether by written, electronic, or other form of communication"
GIVEN form IS A `Form of communication` @desc The form in which the information was published
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376D(2) the means of publication` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN written THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN electronic THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `some other form of communication` THEN JUST TRUE



§§ `s 376E - sexual grooming of minor below 16 years of age`

-- src:8440 | Sexual grooming of minor below 16 years of age
-- src:8442 | 376E.—(1) Any person of or above 18 years of age (A) shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:8443 | if having met or communicated with another person (B) on at least one previous
-- src:8444 | occasion —
-- src:8446 | (a) any of the following acts takes place:
-- src:8447 | (i) A intentionally meets B in Singapore;
-- src:8449 | (ii) A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in
-- src:8450 | Singapore;
-- src:8452 | (iii) A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of
-- src:8453 | meeting B outside Singapore;
-- src:8455 | (iv) B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore
-- src:8456 | which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by
-- src:8457 | implication;
-- src:8459 | (v) B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with
-- src:8460 | A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to
-- src:8461 | whether expressly or by implication; and
-- src:8465 | (b) at the time of the acts referred to in paragraph (a) —
-- src:8466 | (i) A intends, during or after the meeting —
-- src:8468 | (A) to do (in Singapore) anything to or in respect of B
-- src:8469 | which will involve the commission by A of a relevant
-- src:8470 | offence; or
-- src:8472 | (B) to do (outside Singapore) anything to or in respect of B
-- src:8473 | which would, if done in Singapore, involve the
-- src:8474 | commission by A of a relevant offence;
-- src:8478 | (ii) B is below 16 years of age; and
-- src:8481 | (iii) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of
-- src:8482 | age.
-- src:8486 | (2) In subsection (1), “relevant offence” means an offence under —
-- src:8488 | (a) section 354, 354A, 355, 372, 373, 373A, 375, 376, 376A, 376B, 376C,
-- src:8489 | 376EB, 376ED, 376F, 376H, 377(1)(e), (f), (g) or (h), 377B(3), 377BA,
-- src:8490 | 377BB, 377BF, 377BG or 377BH;
-- src:8495 | (b) section 8 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993; or
-- src:8497 | (c) section 140(1) of the Women’s Charter 1961.
-- src:8501 | (3) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial whether the previous occasion of
-- src:8502 | A having met or communicated with B referred to in subsection (1) took place in or
-- src:8503 | outside Singapore.
-- src:8507 | (4) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall on conviction —
-- src:8509 | (a) in the case where the offence is committed against a victim who is below
-- src:8510 | 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above that
-- src:8511 | age, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7
-- src:8512 | years, or with fine, or with both; or
-- src:8516 | (b) in any other case, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- src:8518 | extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- "Relevant offence" (subsection (2), a closed list) is `s 376E(2) the offence is a relevant offence`, below: the two intent leaves are set from it.
-- Subsection (3) makes the place of the previous occasion immaterial; there is no leaf for it.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E (src:8440-8518)
DECLARE `Grooming Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the child (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by travelling to a hotel to meet the said child, intending to have sexual intercourse with her"
    `A is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused (A) of or above 18 years of age? Set from NOT `below 18 years of age` on A's age
    `A has met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had A met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion? It is immaterial whether that occasion was in or outside Singapore (s 376E(3))
    `A intentionally meets B in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A intentionally meet B in Singapore? (s 376E(1)(a)(i))
    `A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A travel in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore? (s 376E(1)(a)(ii))
    `A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A travel from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore? (s 376E(1)(a)(iii))
    `B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does B travel in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to, expressly or by implication? (s 376E(1)(a)(iv))
    `B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does B travel from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to, expressly or by implication? (s 376E(1)(a)(v))
    `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do in Singapore anything to or in respect of B which will involve the commission by A of a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of those acts, did A intend, during or after the meeting, to do (in Singapore) anything to or in respect of B which will involve A committing a relevant offence? The offence must be one of those `s 376E(2) the offence is a relevant offence` lists (s 376E(1)(b)(i)(A))
    `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do outside Singapore anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve the commission by A of a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of those acts, did A intend, during or after the meeting, to do (outside Singapore) anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve A committing a relevant offence? (s 376E(1)(b)(i)(B))
    `B is below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B below 16 years of age at the time of the acts? Set from the helper `below 16 years of age` on B's age (s 376E(1)(b)(ii))
    `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A NOT reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age? (s 376E(1)(b)(iii))
    `B is below 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B below 14 years of age, and does A NOT reasonably believe B is of or above that age? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 376E(4) states (7 years, or 5 years)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E (src:8442-8482)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376E(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual grooming of a minor below 16 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Grooming Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sexually grooms a minor below 16 years of age within section 376E(1)` f IF
        f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  f's `A has met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion`
   ...  "(a) any of the following acts takes place: (i) A intentionally meets B in Singapore; (ii) A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore; (iii) A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore; (iv) B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication; (v) B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally meets B in Singapore` OR f's `A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore` OR f's `A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore` OR f's `B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication` OR f's `B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication`)
   ...  "(b)(i) A intends, during or after the meeting, (A) to do (in Singapore) anything to or in respect of B which will involve the commission by A of a relevant offence; or (B) to do (outside Singapore) anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve the commission by A of a relevant offence"
   ...  (f's `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do in Singapore anything to or in respect of B which will involve the commission by A of a relevant offence` OR f's `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do outside Singapore anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve the commission by A of a relevant offence`)
   ...  f's `B is below 16 years of age`
   ...  f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E(4)(a) (src:8507-8512)
`punishment prescribed by s 376E(4)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376E(4)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E(4)(b) (src:8516-8518)
`punishment prescribed by s 376E(4)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376E(4)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E(4) (src:8507-8518)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376E(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual grooming of a minor below 16 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Grooming Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376E(4)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall on conviction be punished"
   ...  `sexually grooms a minor below 16 years of age within section 376E(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Grooming Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of sexual grooming of minor below 16 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`) "A is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A has met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion`) "A has met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion"),
        (`missing unless` ((f's `A intentionally meets B in Singapore` OR f's `A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore` OR f's `A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore` OR f's `B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication` OR f's `B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication`)) "one of the five meeting acts takes place"),
        (`missing unless` ((f's `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do in Singapore anything to or in respect of B which will involve the commission by A of a relevant offence` OR f's `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do outside Singapore anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve the commission by A of a relevant offence`)) "A intends, during or after the meeting, to do anything to or in respect of B which would involve A committing a relevant offence"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is below 16 years of age`) "B is below 16 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age`) "A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376E(4)` f) "the elements of section 376E(4) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E(4) (src:8507-8518)
@export Frame a charge under section 376E(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual grooming of a minor below 16 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Grooming Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376E(4)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376E(4)" "sexual grooming of minor below 16 years of age"
        (IF f's `B is below 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 376E(4)(a)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 376E(4)(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376E(4)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 18 years of age, having met or communicated with ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 16 years of age, on at least one previous occasion, did, with the intention of doing in respect of the said person something that would involve the commission by you of a relevant offence, and not reasonably believing the said person to be of or above 16 years of age, bring about a meeting between you and the said person, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of sexual grooming of minor below 16 years of age not made out` f)

-- 376E(2)(a), 376EA(2)(a): the relevant offences of the Penal Code (a closed list, "means")
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E(2)(a) (src:8488-8490)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the offences relevant under section 376E(2)` MEANS
    LIST "354", "354A", "355", "372", "373", "373A", "375", "376", "376A", "376B", "376C",
         "376EB", "376ED", "376F", "376H",
         "377(1)(e)", "377(1)(f)", "377(1)(g)", "377(1)(h)", "377B(3)",
         "377BA", "377BB", "377BF", "377BG", "377BH"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376E(2) (src:8486-8497)
@export Whether an offence is a "relevant offence" within section 376E(2) of the Penal Code 1871: an offence under the listed sections of the Code, section 8 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993, or section 140(1) of the Women's Charter 1961
GIVEN offence IS A STRING @desc The offence A intends to commit, cited as the section of the Penal Code 1871 ("375", "377(1)(e)"), or as "Children and Young Persons Act 1993 s 8" or "Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)"; any other text is another offence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376E(2) the offence is a relevant offence` MEANS
    IF elem offence (`the offences relevant under section 376E(2)`)
        OR offence EQUALS "Children and Young Persons Act 1993 s 8"
        OR offence EQUALS "Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"relevant offence\" means an offence under — ..." (a closed list)



§§ `s 376EA - exploitative sexual grooming of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`

-- src:8523 | Exploitative sexual grooming of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age
-- src:8525 | 376EA.—(1) Any person of or above 18 years of age (A) shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:8526 | if having met or communicated with another person (B) on at least one previous
-- src:8527 | occasion —
-- src:8529 | (a) any of the following acts takes place:
-- src:8530 | (i) A intentionally meets B in Singapore;
-- src:8532 | (ii) A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in
-- src:8533 | Singapore;
-- src:8536 | (iii) A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of
-- src:8537 | meeting B outside Singapore;
-- src:8539 | (iv) B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore
-- src:8540 | which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by
-- src:8541 | implication;
-- src:8543 | (v) B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with
-- src:8544 | A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to
-- src:8545 | whether expressly or by implication; and
-- src:8549 | (b) at the time of the acts mentioned in paragraph (a) —
-- src:8551 | (i) A intends, during or after the meeting —
-- src:8553 | (A) to do (in Singapore) anything to or in respect of B
-- src:8554 | which will involve the commission by A of a relevant
-- src:8555 | offence; or
-- src:8557 | (B) to do (outside Singapore) anything to or in respect of B
-- src:8558 | which would, if done in Singapore, involve the
-- src:8559 | commission by A of a relevant offence;
-- src:8563 | (ii) B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age;
-- src:8565 | (iii) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of
-- src:8566 | age; and
-- src:8568 | (iv) A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B.
-- src:8572 | (2) In subsection (1), “relevant offence” means an offence under —
-- src:8574 | (a) section 354, 354A, 355, 372, 373, 373A, 375, 376, 376AA, 376B, 376C,
-- src:8575 | 376EC, 376EE, 376F, 376G, 376H, 377(1)(e), (f), (g) or (h), 377B(3),
-- src:8576 | 377BA, 377BB, 377BF or 377BL;
-- src:8581 | (b) section 140(1) of the Women’s Charter 1961; or
-- src:8586 | (c) section 8 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993.
-- src:8592 | (3) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial whether the previous occasion of
-- src:8593 | A having met or communicated with B mentioned in subsection (1) took place in or
-- src:8594 | outside Singapore.
-- src:8598 | (4) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with
-- src:8599 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- "Relevant offence" (subsection (2), a closed list) is `s 376EA(2) the offence is a relevant offence`, below.
-- Subsection (3) makes the place of the previous occasion immaterial; there is no leaf for it.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA (src:8523-8599)
DECLARE `Exploitative Grooming Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the child (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by travelling to a flat to meet the said child, intending to have sexual intercourse with her"
    `A is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused (A) of or above 18 years of age? Set from NOT `below 18 years of age` on A's age
    `A has met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had A met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion? It is immaterial whether that occasion was in or outside Singapore (s 376EA(3))
    `A intentionally meets B in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A intentionally meet B in Singapore? (s 376EA(1)(a)(i))
    `A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A travel in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore? (s 376EA(1)(a)(ii))
    `A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A travel from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore? (s 376EA(1)(a)(iii))
    `B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does B travel in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to, expressly or by implication? (s 376EA(1)(a)(iv))
    `B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does B travel from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to, expressly or by implication? (s 376EA(1)(a)(v))
    `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do in Singapore anything to or in respect of B which will involve the commission by A of a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of those acts, did A intend, during or after the meeting, to do (in Singapore) anything to or in respect of B which will involve A committing a relevant offence? The offence must be one of those `s 376EA(2) the offence is a relevant offence` lists (s 376EA(1)(b)(i)(A))
    `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do outside Singapore anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve the commission by A of a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of those acts, did A intend, during or after the meeting, to do (outside Singapore) anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve A committing a relevant offence? (s 376EA(1)(b)(i)(B))
    `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B of or above 16 but below 18 years of age at the time of the acts? Set from the helper `of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age` on B's age (s 376EA(1)(b)(ii))
    `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A NOT reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age? (s 376EA(1)(b)(iii))
    `A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is A in a relationship that is exploitative of B, as the court determines under s 377CA? (s 376EA(1)(b)(iv))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA (src:8525-8568)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376EA(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual grooming of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Grooming Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exploitatively sexually grooms a minor within section 376EA(1)` f IF
        f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  f's `A has met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion`
   ...  "(a) any of the following acts takes place: (i) A intentionally meets B in Singapore; (ii) A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore; (iii) A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore; (iv) B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication; (v) B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally meets B in Singapore` OR f's `A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore` OR f's `A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore` OR f's `B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication` OR f's `B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication`)
   ...  "(b)(i) A intends, during or after the meeting, (A) to do (in Singapore) anything to or in respect of B which will involve the commission by A of a relevant offence; or (B) to do (outside Singapore) anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve the commission by A of a relevant offence"
   ...  (f's `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do in Singapore anything to or in respect of B which will involve the commission by A of a relevant offence` OR f's `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do outside Singapore anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve the commission by A of a relevant offence`)
   ...  f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`
   ...  f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  f's `A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA(4) (src:8598-8599)
`punishment prescribed by s 376EA(4)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376EA(4)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA(4) (src:8598-8599)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376EA(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual grooming of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Grooming Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376EA(4)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
   ...  `exploitatively sexually grooms a minor within section 376EA(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Grooming Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of exploitative sexual grooming of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`) "A is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A has met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion`) "A has met or communicated with B on at least one previous occasion"),
        (`missing unless` ((f's `A intentionally meets B in Singapore` OR f's `A travels in Singapore with the intention of meeting B in Singapore` OR f's `A travels from a location in Singapore with the intention of meeting B outside Singapore` OR f's `B travels in Singapore to attend a meeting with A in Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication` OR f's `B travels from a location in Singapore to attend a meeting with A outside Singapore which A has either initiated or agreed to whether expressly or by implication`)) "one of the five meeting acts takes place"),
        (`missing unless` ((f's `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do in Singapore anything to or in respect of B which will involve the commission by A of a relevant offence` OR f's `A intends, during or after the meeting, to do outside Singapore anything to or in respect of B which would, if done in Singapore, involve the commission by A of a relevant offence`)) "A intends, during or after the meeting, to do anything to or in respect of B which would involve A committing a relevant offence"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`) "B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age`) "A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B`) "A is in a relationship that is exploitative of B"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376EA(4)` f) "the elements of section 376EA(4) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA(4) (src:8598-8599)
@export Frame a charge under section 376EA(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual grooming of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Grooming Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376EA(4)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376EA(4)" "exploitative sexual grooming of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376EA(4)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376EA(4)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 18 years of age, in a relationship that is exploitative of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, having met or communicated with the said person on at least one previous occasion, did, with the intention of doing in respect of the said person something that would involve the commission by you of a relevant offence, and not reasonably believing the said person to be of or above 18 years of age, bring about a meeting between you and the said person, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of exploitative sexual grooming of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA(2)(a) (src:8574-8576)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the offences relevant under section 376EA(2)` MEANS
    LIST "354", "354A", "355", "372", "373", "373A", "375", "376", "376AA", "376B", "376C",
         "376EC", "376EE", "376F", "376G", "376H",
         "377(1)(e)", "377(1)(f)", "377(1)(g)", "377(1)(h)", "377B(3)",
         "377BA", "377BB", "377BF", "377BL"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EA(2) (src:8572-8586)
@export Whether an offence is a "relevant offence" within section 376EA(2) of the Penal Code 1871: an offence under the listed sections of the Code, section 140(1) of the Women's Charter 1961, or section 8 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993
GIVEN offence IS A STRING @desc The offence A intends to commit, cited as the section of the Penal Code 1871 ("375", "377(1)(e)"), or as "Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)" or "Children and Young Persons Act 1993 s 8"; any other text is another offence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376EA(2) the offence is a relevant offence` MEANS
    IF elem offence (`the offences relevant under section 376EA(2)`)
        OR offence EQUALS "Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)"
        OR offence EQUALS "Children and Young Persons Act 1993 s 8"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"relevant offence\" means an offence under — ..." (a closed list)



§§ `s 376EB - sexual communication with minor below 16 years of age`

-- src:8604 | Sexual communication with minor below 16 years of age
-- src:8606 | 376EB.—(1) Any person of or above 18 years of age (A) shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:8607 | if —
-- src:8609 | (a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another
-- src:8610 | person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally communicated
-- src:8611 | with B;
-- src:8613 | (b) the communication is sexual;
-- src:8615 | (c) at the time of the communication, B is below 16 years of age; and
-- src:8617 | (d) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age.
-- src:8621 | (2) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial —
-- src:8623 | (a) whether B replied or responded to A’s communication mentioned in
-- src:8624 | subsection (1); and
-- src:8626 | (b) whether such communication originated in Singapore provided that either
-- src:8627 | A or B was in Singapore at the time of such communication.
-- src:8631 | (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall —
-- src:8633 | (a) in the case where the offence is committed against a victim who is below
-- src:8634 | 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above that
-- src:8635 | age, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- src:8636 | 3 years, or with fine, or with both; or
-- src:8638 | (b) in any other case, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- src:8639 | extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- src:8643 | (4) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for any communication
-- src:8644 | with his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse.
-- Subsection (2)(a): whether B replied is immaterial, so the leaf is carried and ignored (FORK DEF-B3).
-- Subsection (2)(b): where the communication originated is immaterial "provided that either A or B was in Singapore", read as a condition (FORK DEF-B3).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EB (src:8604-8644)
DECLARE `Sexual Communication Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the child (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by sending the said child messages describing sexual acts"
    `A is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused (A) of or above 18 years of age? Set from NOT `below 18 years of age` on A's age
    `A intentionally communicated with B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally communicate with B? (s 376EB(1)(a))
    `A communicated for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of the communication to obtain sexual gratification? (s 376EB(1)(a))
    `A communicated for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of the communication to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 376EB(1)(a))
    `the communication is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication sexual - as s 377C(3)(d) says when a communication is sexual? (s 376EB(1)(b)) See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
    `B is below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was B below 16 years of age at the time of the communication? Set from the helper `below 16 years of age` on B's age (s 376EB(1)(c))
    `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A NOT reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age? (s 376EB(1)(d))
    `either A or B was in Singapore at the time of the communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was either A or B in Singapore at the time of the communication? Where the communication originated is immaterial, provided that this is so (s 376EB(2)(b))
    `B replied or responded to A's communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B reply or respond to A's communication? NOT an element: s 376EB(2)(a) says it is immaterial, so the answer changes nothing
    `the communication was with the accused's spouse with the consent of that spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the communication with A's spouse, with that spouse's consent? (s 376EB(4): then there is no offence under the section)
    `B is below 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B below 14 years of age, and does A NOT reasonably believe B is of or above that age? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 376EB(3) states (3 years, or 2 years)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EB (src:8606-8617)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376EB(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual communication with a minor below 16 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Communication Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sexually communicates with a minor below 16 years of age within section 376EB(1)` f IF
        f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  "(a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally communicated with B"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally communicated with B` AND (f's `A communicated for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A communicated for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`))
   ...  "(b) the communication is sexual"
   ...  f's `the communication is sexual`
   ...  "(c) at the time of the communication, B is below 16 years of age; and (d) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age"
   ...  (f's `B is below 16 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age`)
   ...  "(2)(b) whether such communication originated in Singapore provided that either A or B was in Singapore at the time of such communication"
   ...  f's `either A or B was in Singapore at the time of the communication`
   ...  "(4) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for any communication with his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse"
   ...  (NOT (f's `the communication was with the accused's spouse with the consent of that spouse`))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for any communication with his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EB(3)(a) (src:8631-8636)
`punishment prescribed by s 376EB(3)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376EB(3)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EB(3)(b) (src:8638-8639)
`punishment prescribed by s 376EB(3)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376EB(3)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EB(3) (src:8631-8639)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376EB(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual communication with a minor below 16 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Communication Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376EB(3)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished"
   ...  `sexually communicates with a minor below 16 years of age within section 376EB(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Communication Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of sexual communication with minor below 16 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`) "A is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally communicated with B` AND (f's `A communicated for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A communicated for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`)) "for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally communicated with B"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the communication is sexual`) "the communication is sexual"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is below 16 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age`) "at the time of the communication B is below 16 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `either A or B was in Singapore at the time of the communication`) "either A or B was in Singapore at the time of the communication"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `the communication was with the accused's spouse with the consent of that spouse`)) "the communication was not with the accused's spouse with that spouse's consent (section 376EB(4))"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376EB(3)` f) "the elements of section 376EB(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EB(3) (src:8631-8639)
@export Frame a charge under section 376EB(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual communication with a minor below 16 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Communication Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376EB(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376EB(3)" "sexual communication with minor below 16 years of age"
        (IF f's `B is below 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 376EB(3)(a)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 376EB(3)(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376EB(3)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 18 years of age, for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing humiliation, alarm or distress to ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 16 years of age, did intentionally communicate with the said person in a sexual communication, not reasonably believing the said person to be of or above 16 years of age, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of sexual communication with minor below 16 years of age not made out` f)


§§ `s 376EC - exploitative sexual communication with minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`

-- src:8649 | Exploitative sexual communication with minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of
-- src:8650 | age
-- src:8652 | 376EC.—(1) Any person of or above 18 years of age (A) shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:8653 | if —
-- src:8655 | (a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another
-- src:8656 | person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally communicated
-- src:8657 | with B;
-- src:8659 | (b) the communication is sexual;
-- src:8661 | (c) at the time of the communication, B is of or above 16 but below 18 years
-- src:8662 | of age;
-- src:8664 | (d) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age; and
-- src:8666 | (e) B is in a relationship with A that is exploitative of B.
-- src:8670 | (2) For the purposes of this section, it is immaterial —
-- src:8672 | (a) whether B replied or responded to A’s communication mentioned in
-- src:8673 | subsection (1); and
-- src:8675 | (b) whether such communication originated in Singapore provided that either
-- src:8676 | A or B was in Singapore at the time of such communication.
-- src:8680 | (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with
-- src:8681 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- Subsection (2) is carried as in s 376EB (FORK DEF-B3).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EC (src:8649-8681)
DECLARE `Exploitative Sexual Communication Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the child (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by sending the said child messages describing sexual acts"
    `A is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused (A) of or above 18 years of age? Set from NOT `below 18 years of age` on A's age
    `A intentionally communicated with B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally communicate with B? (s 376EC(1)(a))
    `A communicated for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of the communication to obtain sexual gratification? (s 376EC(1)(a))
    `A communicated for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of the communication to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 376EC(1)(a))
    `the communication is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication sexual - as s 377C(3)(d) says when a communication is sexual? (s 376EC(1)(b)) See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
    `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was B of or above 16 but below 18 years of age at the time of the communication? Set from the helper `of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age` on B's age (s 376EC(1)(c))
    `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A NOT reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age? (s 376EC(1)(d))
    `B is in a relationship with A that is exploitative of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B in a relationship with A that is exploitative of B, as the court determines under s 377CA? (s 376EC(1)(e))
    `either A or B was in Singapore at the time of the communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was either A or B in Singapore at the time of the communication? Where the communication originated is immaterial, provided that this is so (s 376EC(2)(b))
    `B replied or responded to A's communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B reply or respond to A's communication? NOT an element: s 376EC(2)(a) says it is immaterial, so the answer changes nothing

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EC (src:8652-8666)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376EC(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual communication with a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Communication Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exploitatively sexually communicates with a minor within section 376EC(1)` f IF
        f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  "(a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally communicated with B"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally communicated with B` AND (f's `A communicated for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A communicated for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`))
   ...  "(b) the communication is sexual"
   ...  f's `the communication is sexual`
   ...  "(c) at the time of the communication, B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age; (d) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age; and (e) B is in a relationship with A that is exploitative of B"
   ...  (f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` AND f's `B is in a relationship with A that is exploitative of B`)
   ...  "(2)(b) whether such communication originated in Singapore provided that either A or B was in Singapore at the time of such communication"
   ...  f's `either A or B was in Singapore at the time of the communication`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EC(3) (src:8680-8681)
`punishment prescribed by s 376EC(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376EC(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EC(3) (src:8680-8681)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376EC(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual communication with a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Communication Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376EC(3)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
   ...  `exploitatively sexually communicates with a minor within section 376EC(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Communication Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of exploitative sexual communication with minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`) "A is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally communicated with B` AND (f's `A communicated for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A communicated for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`)) "for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally communicated with B"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the communication is sexual`) "the communication is sexual"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` AND f's `B is in a relationship with A that is exploitative of B`) "at the time of the communication B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, A does not reasonably believe B is of or above 18, and B is in a relationship with A that is exploitative of B"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `either A or B was in Singapore at the time of the communication`) "either A or B was in Singapore at the time of the communication"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376EC(3)` f) "the elements of section 376EC(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EC(3) (src:8680-8681)
@export Frame a charge under section 376EC(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual communication with a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Communication Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376EC(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376EC(3)" "exploitative sexual communication with minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376EC(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376EC(3)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 18 years of age, in a relationship that is exploitative of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing humiliation, alarm or distress to the said person, did intentionally communicate with the said person in a sexual communication, not reasonably believing the said person to be of or above 18 years of age, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of exploitative sexual communication with minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age not made out` f)


§§ `s 376ED - sexual activity or image in presence of minor below 16 years of age`

-- src:8685 | Sexual activity or image in presence of minor below 16 years of age
-- src:8687 | 376ED.—(1) Any person of or above 18 years of age (A) shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:8688 | if —
-- src:8690 | (a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another
-- src:8691 | person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally engages in an
-- src:8692 | activity;
-- src:8694 | (b) the activity is sexual;
-- src:8696 | (c) A engages in the activity —
-- src:8697 | (i) when B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed;
-- src:8699 | (ii) when either A or B is or both are in Singapore; and
-- src:8702 | (iii) knowing or believing that B is aware, or intending that B should
-- src:8703 | be aware, that A is engaging in it;
-- src:8705 | (d) B is below 16 years of age; and
-- src:8707 | (e) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age.
-- src:8711 | (2) Any person of or above 18 years of age (A) shall be guilty of an offence if —
-- src:8713 | (a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another
-- src:8714 | person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally causes B to
-- src:8715 | observe an image;
-- src:8717 | (b) the image is sexual;
-- src:8719 | (c) B is below 16 years of age;
-- src:8721 | (d) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age; and
-- src:8723 | (e) either A or B is or both are in Singapore.
-- src:8727 | (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall —
-- src:8729 | (a) in the case where the offence is committed against a victim who is below
-- src:8730 | 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above that
-- src:8731 | age, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- src:8732 | 3 years, or with fine, or with both; or
-- src:8734 | (b) in any other case, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- src:8736 | extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- src:8741 | (4) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section against B if B is his or
-- src:8742 | her spouse with the consent of that spouse.
-- Two offences, (1) activity and (2) image, one punishment, (3) (FORK DEF-B4: subsection (4)'s spouse bar is read as covering both).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED (src:8685-8742)
DECLARE `Sexual Activity Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the child (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by masturbating in front of the said child"
    `A is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused (A) of or above 18 years of age? Set from NOT `below 18 years of age` on A's age
    `A intentionally engages in an activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally engage in an activity? (s 376ED(1)(a))
    `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of A's engaging in the activity to obtain sexual gratification? (s 376ED(1)(a))
    `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of A's engaging in the activity to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 376ED(1)(a))
    `the activity is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the activity sexual - as s 377C(3)(d) says when an activity is sexual? (s 376ED(1)(b)) See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
    `B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A engage in it when B was present or in a place from which A could be observed? (s 376ED(1)(c)(i))
    `either A or B is or both are in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was either A or B, or were both, in Singapore? (s 376ED(1)(c)(ii), (2)(e))
    `A knows or believes that B is aware, or intends that B should be aware, that A is engaging in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or believe that B was aware, or intend that B should be aware, that A was engaging in it? (s 376ED(1)(c)(iii))
    `A intentionally causes B to observe an image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally cause B to observe an image? (s 376ED(2)(a))
    `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of A's causing B to observe the image to obtain sexual gratification? (s 376ED(2)(a))
    `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of A's causing B to observe the image to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 376ED(2)(a))
    `the image is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image sexual - as s 377C(3)(d) says when an image is sexual? (s 376ED(2)(b)) See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
    `B is below 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B below 16 years of age? Set from the helper `below 16 years of age` on B's age (s 376ED(1)(d), (2)(c))
    `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A NOT reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age? (s 376ED(1)(e), (2)(d))
    `B is the accused's spouse and consented to the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B A's spouse, and did that spouse consent to the activity or to observing the image? (s 376ED(4): then there is no offence under the section against B)
    `B is below 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B below 14 years of age, and does A NOT reasonably believe B is of or above that age? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 376ED(3) states (3 years, or 2 years)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED (src:8687-8707)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376ED(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual activity in the presence of a minor below 16 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `engages in a sexual activity in the presence of a minor below 16 years of age within section 376ED(1)` f IF
        f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  "(a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally engages in an activity"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally engages in an activity` AND (f's `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`))
   ...  "(b) the activity is sexual"
   ...  f's `the activity is sexual`
   ...  "(c) A engages in the activity (i) when B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed; (ii) when either A or B is or both are in Singapore; and (iii) knowing or believing that B is aware, or intending that B should be aware, that A is engaging in it"
   ...  (f's `B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed` AND f's `either A or B is or both are in Singapore` AND f's `A knows or believes that B is aware, or intends that B should be aware, that A is engaging in it`)
   ...  "(d) B is below 16 years of age; and (e) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age"
   ...  (f's `B is below 16 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age`)
   ...  "(4) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section against B if B is his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse"
   ...  (NOT (f's `B is the accused's spouse and consented to the activity`))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section against B if B is his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED (src:8711-8723)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376ED(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing a minor below 16 years of age to observe a sexual image)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `causes a minor below 16 years of age to observe a sexual image within section 376ED(2)` f IF
        f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  "(a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally causes B to observe an image"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally causes B to observe an image` AND (f's `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`))
   ...  "(b) the image is sexual"
   ...  f's `the image is sexual`
   ...  "(c) B is below 16 years of age; (d) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age; and (e) either A or B is or both are in Singapore"
   ...  (f's `B is below 16 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age` AND f's `either A or B is or both are in Singapore`)
   ...  "(4) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section against B if B is his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse"
   ...  (NOT (f's `B is the accused's spouse and consented to the activity`))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section against B if B is his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED(3)(a) (src:8727-8732)
`punishment prescribed by s 376ED(3)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376ED(3)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED(3)(b) (src:8734-8736)
`punishment prescribed by s 376ED(3)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376ED(3)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED(1) (src:8727-8736)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376ED(3) of the Penal Code 1871 by a sexual activity in the presence of a minor below 16 years of age
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376ED(1)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished"
   ...  `engages in a sexual activity in the presence of a minor below 16 years of age within section 376ED(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Activity Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of sexual activity in presence of minor below 16 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`) "A is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally engages in an activity` AND (f's `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`)) "for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally engages in an activity"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the activity is sexual`) "the activity is sexual"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed` AND f's `either A or B is or both are in Singapore` AND f's `A knows or believes that B is aware, or intends that B should be aware, that A is engaging in it`) "A engages in the activity when B is present or can observe A, when either or both are in Singapore, knowing or believing that B is aware, or intending that B should be aware"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is below 16 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age`) "B is below 16 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `B is the accused's spouse and consented to the activity`)) "B is not the accused's spouse consenting (section 376ED(4))"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376ED(1)` f) "the elements of section 376ED(1) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED(1) (src:8727-8736)
@export Frame a charge under section 376ED(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual activity in the presence of a minor below 16 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376ED(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376ED(1)" "sexual activity in presence of minor below 16 years of age"
        (IF f's `B is below 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 376ED(3)(a)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 376ED(3)(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376ED(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 18 years of age, for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing humiliation, alarm or distress to ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 16 years of age, did intentionally engage in a sexual activity when the said person was present or in a place from which you could be observed, knowing or believing, or intending, that the said person was aware of it, not reasonably believing the said person to be of or above 16 years of age, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of sexual activity in presence of minor below 16 years of age not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED(2) (src:8727-8736)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376ED(3) of the Penal Code 1871 by causing a minor below 16 years of age to observe a sexual image
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376ED(2)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished"
   ...  `causes a minor below 16 years of age to observe a sexual image within section 376ED(2)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Activity Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of causing minor below 16 years of age to observe a sexual image not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`) "A is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally causes B to observe an image` AND (f's `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`)) "for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally causes B to observe an image"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the image is sexual`) "the image is sexual"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is below 16 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 16 years of age` AND f's `either A or B is or both are in Singapore`) "B is below 16 years of age, A does not reasonably believe B is of or above 16, and either or both are in Singapore"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `B is the accused's spouse and consented to the activity`)) "B is not the accused's spouse consenting (section 376ED(4))"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376ED(2)` f) "the elements of section 376ED(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376ED(2) (src:8727-8736)
@export Frame a charge under section 376ED(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing a minor below 16 years of age to observe a sexual image), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376ED(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376ED(2)" "causing minor below 16 years of age to observe a sexual image"
        (IF f's `B is below 14 years of age and A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 14 years of age` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 376ED(3)(a)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 376ED(3)(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376ED(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 18 years of age, for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing humiliation, alarm or distress to ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person below 16 years of age, did intentionally cause the said person to observe a sexual image, not reasonably believing the said person to be of or above 16 years of age, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of causing minor below 16 years of age to observe a sexual image not made out` f)


§§ `s 376EE - exploitative sexual activity or image in presence of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`

-- src:8746 | Exploitative sexual activity or image in presence of minor of or above 16 but below
-- src:8747 | 18 years of age
-- src:8749 | 376EE.—(1) Any person of or above 18 years of age (A) shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:8750 | if —
-- src:8752 | (a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another
-- src:8753 | person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally engages in an
-- src:8754 | activity;
-- src:8757 | (b) the activity is sexual;
-- src:8758 | (c) A engages in the activity —
-- src:8760 | (i) when B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed;
-- src:8762 | (ii) when either A or B is or both are in Singapore; and
-- src:8764 | (iii) knowing or believing that B is aware, or intending that B should
-- src:8765 | be aware, that A is engaging in it;
-- src:8767 | (d) B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age;
-- src:8769 | (e) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age; and
-- src:8771 | (f) A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B.
-- src:8775 | (2) Any person of or above 18 years of age (A) shall be guilty of an offence if —
-- src:8777 | (a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another
-- src:8778 | person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally causes B to
-- src:8779 | observe an image;
-- src:8781 | (b) the image is sexual;
-- src:8783 | (c) B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age;
-- src:8785 | (d) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age;
-- src:8787 | (e) A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B; and
-- src:8789 | (f) either A or B is or both are in Singapore.
-- src:8793 | (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with
-- src:8795 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- Two offences, (1) activity and (2) image, one punishment, (3).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EE (src:8746-8795)
DECLARE `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the child (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by showing the said child a pornographic film"
    `A is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused (A) of or above 18 years of age? Set from NOT `below 18 years of age` on A's age
    `A intentionally engages in an activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally engage in an activity? (s 376EE(1)(a))
    `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of A's engaging in the activity to obtain sexual gratification? (s 376EE(1)(a))
    `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of A's engaging in the activity to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 376EE(1)(a))
    `the activity is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the activity sexual - as s 377C(3)(d) says? (s 376EE(1)(b)) See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
    `B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A engage in it when B was present or in a place from which A could be observed? (s 376EE(1)(c)(i))
    `either A or B is or both are in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was either A or B, or were both, in Singapore? (s 376EE(1)(c)(ii), (2)(f))
    `A knows or believes that B is aware, or intends that B should be aware, that A is engaging in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know or believe that B was aware, or intend that B should be aware, that A was engaging in it? (s 376EE(1)(c)(iii))
    `A intentionally causes B to observe an image` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally cause B to observe an image? (s 376EE(2)(a))
    `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of A's causing B to observe the image to obtain sexual gratification? (s 376EE(2)(a))
    `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of A's causing B to observe the image to cause B humiliation, alarm or distress? (s 376EE(2)(a))
    `the image is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the image sexual - as s 377C(3)(d) says? (s 376EE(2)(b)) See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
    `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B of or above 16 but below 18 years of age? Set from the helper `of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age` on B's age (s 376EE(1)(d), (2)(c))
    `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A NOT reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age? (s 376EE(1)(e), (2)(d))
    `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is A in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B, as the court determines under s 377CA? (s 376EE(1)(f), (2)(e))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EE (src:8749-8771)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376EE(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual activity in the presence of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age in an exploitative relationship)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `engages in a sexual activity in the presence of a minor in an exploitative relationship within section 376EE(1)` f IF
        f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  "(a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally engages in an activity"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally engages in an activity` AND (f's `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`))
   ...  "(b) the activity is sexual"
   ...  f's `the activity is sexual`
   ...  "(c) A engages in the activity (i) when B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed; (ii) when either A or B is or both are in Singapore; and (iii) knowing or believing that B is aware, or intending that B should be aware, that A is engaging in it"
   ...  (f's `B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed` AND f's `either A or B is or both are in Singapore` AND f's `A knows or believes that B is aware, or intends that B should be aware, that A is engaging in it`)
   ...  "(d) B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age; (e) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age; and (f) A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B"
   ...  (f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` AND f's `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EE (src:8775-8789)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376EE(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age in an exploitative relationship to observe a sexual image)
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
