        f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  "(a) for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing another person (B) humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally causes B to observe an image"
   ...  (f's `A intentionally causes B to observe an image` AND (f's `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`))
   ...  "(b) the image is sexual"
   ...  f's `the image is sexual`
   ...  "(c) B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age; (d) A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age; (e) A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B; and (f) either A or B is or both are in Singapore"
   ...  (f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` AND f's `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B` AND f's `either A or B is or both are in Singapore`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EE(3) (src:8793-8795)
`punishment prescribed by s 376EE(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376EE(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EE(1) (src:8793-8795)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376EE(3) of the Penal Code 1871 by a sexual activity in the presence of a minor in an exploitative relationship
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376EE(1)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
   ...  `engages in a sexual activity in the presence of a minor in an exploitative relationship within section 376EE(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of exploitative sexual activity in presence of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`) "A is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally engages in an activity` AND (f's `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A engaged in the activity for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`)) "for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally engages in an activity"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the activity is sexual`) "the activity is sexual"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is present or is in a place from which A can be observed` AND f's `either A or B is or both are in Singapore` AND f's `A knows or believes that B is aware, or intends that B should be aware, that A is engaging in it`) "A engages in the activity when B is present or can observe A, when either or both are in Singapore, knowing or believing that B is aware, or intending that B should be aware"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` AND f's `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B`) "B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, A does not reasonably believe B is of or above 18, and A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376EE(1)` f) "the elements of section 376EE(1) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EE(1) (src:8793-8795)
@export Frame a charge under section 376EE(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual activity in the presence of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376EE(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376EE(1)" "exploitative sexual activity in presence of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376EE(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376EE(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 18 years of age, in a relationship that is exploitative of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing humiliation, alarm or distress to the said person, did intentionally engage in a sexual activity when the said person was present or in a place from which you could be observed, knowing or believing, or intending, that the said person was aware of it, not reasonably believing the said person to be of or above 18 years of age, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of exploitative sexual activity in presence of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EE(2) (src:8793-8795)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376EE(3) of the Penal Code 1871 by causing a minor in an exploitative relationship to observe a sexual image
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376EE(2)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
   ...  `causes a minor in an exploitative relationship to observe a sexual image within section 376EE(2)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of exploitative causing of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age to observe a sexual image not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 18 years of age`) "A is of or above 18 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally causes B to observe an image` AND (f's `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification` OR f's `A caused B to observe the image for the purpose of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress`)) "for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing B humiliation, alarm or distress, A intentionally causes B to observe an image"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the image is sexual`) "the image is sexual"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age` AND f's `A does not reasonably believe that B is of or above 18 years of age` AND f's `A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B` AND f's `either A or B is or both are in Singapore`) "B is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, A does not reasonably believe B is of or above 18, A is in a relationship with B that is exploitative of B, and either or both are in Singapore"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376EE(2)` f) "the elements of section 376EE(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376EE(2) (src:8793-8795)
@export Frame a charge under section 376EE(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative causing of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age to observe a sexual image), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Exploitative Sexual Activity Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376EE(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376EE(2)" "exploitative causing of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age to observe a sexual image"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376EE(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376EE(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 18 years of age, in a relationship that is exploitative of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person of or above 16 but below 18 years of age, for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing humiliation, alarm or distress to the said person, did intentionally cause the said person to observe a sexual image, not reasonably believing the said person to be of or above 18 years of age, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of exploitative causing of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age to observe a sexual image not made out` f)


§§ `s 376F - procurement of sexual activity with person with mental disability`

-- src:8800 | Procurement of sexual activity with person with mental disability
-- src:8801 | 376F.—(1) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence if —
-- src:8802 | (a) A intentionally touches another person (B) or intentionally incites B to
-- src:8803 | touch A or B or another person;
-- src:8804 | (b) the touching is sexual and B consents to the touching;
-- src:8805 | (c) A obtains B’s consent —
-- src:8808 | (i) where B is not A’s spouse, by means of an inducement offered
-- src:8809 | or given, a threat made or a deception practised by A for that
-- src:8810 | purpose; or
-- src:8812 | (ii) where B is A’s spouse, by means of a threat made or a deception
-- src:8813 | practised by A for that purpose;
-- src:8815 | (ca) B has a mental disability; and
-- src:8817 | (d) A knows or could reasonably be expected to know that B has a mental
-- src:8818 | disability.
-- src:8822 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), a person who is guilty of an offence under this section
-- src:8823 | shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with
-- src:8824 | fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments.
-- src:8828 | (3) If the touching involved —
-- src:8830 | (a) penetration of the vagina or anus, as the case may be, with a part of the
-- src:8831 | body or anything else; or
-- src:8833 | (b) penetration of the mouth with the penis,
-- src:8835 | a person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with
-- src:8836 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to a fine
-- src:8837 | or to caning.
-- src:8841 | (4) [Deleted by Act 15 of 2019]
-- src:8843 | (5) For the purposes of this section, “mental disability” means an impairment of or a
-- src:8844 | disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain resulting from any disability or
-- src:8845 | disorder of the mind or brain which impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the
-- src:8846 | giving of consent to sexual touching.
-- "Mental disability" (subsection (5), "means") is `s 376F(5) the impairment is a mental disability`, below.
-- Subsection (2) is "subject to subsection (3)": the offence under (2) is the one whose touching involved no such penetration (FORK DEF-B5).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F (src:8800-8846)
DECLARE `Mental Disability Procurement Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person touched (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by threatening to withhold the said person's allowance unless the said person agreed to be touched"
    `A intentionally touches B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally touch B? (s 376F(1)(a))
    `A intentionally incites B to touch A or B or another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally incite B to touch A or B or another person? (s 376F(1)(a))
    `the touching is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the touching sexual - as s 377C(3)(d) says? (s 376F(1)(b)) See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
    `B consents to the touching` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B consent to the touching? (s 376F(1)(b))
    `B is not A's spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B NOT A's spouse? (s 376F(1)(c)(i))
    `B is A's spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B A's spouse? (s 376F(1)(c)(ii))
    `A obtains B's consent by means of an inducement offered or given by A for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A obtain B's consent by means of an inducement offered or given by A for that purpose? Counts only where B is not A's spouse (s 376F(1)(c)(i))
    `A obtains B's consent by means of a threat made by A for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A obtain B's consent by means of a threat made by A for that purpose? (s 376F(1)(c)(i), (ii))
    `A obtains B's consent by means of a deception practised by A for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A obtain B's consent by means of a deception practised by A for that purpose? (s 376F(1)(c)(i), (ii))
    `B has a mental disability within section 376F(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does B have a mental disability as s 376F(5) gives the meaning - an impairment of or disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain, resulting from a disability or disorder of the mind or brain, which impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in giving consent to sexual touching? Set from `s 376F(5) the impairment is a mental disability` (s 376F(1)(ca))
    `A knows or could reasonably be expected to know that B has a mental disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know, or could A reasonably be expected to know, that B has a mental disability? (s 376F(1)(d))
    `the touching involved penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the touching involve penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis? NOT an element: it chooses between s 376F(2) (5 years) and s 376F(3) (20 years)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F (src:8801-8818)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376F(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (procuring a sexual touching, to which a person with a mental disability consents, by inducement, threat or deception)
GIVEN f IS A `Mental Disability Procurement Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `procures sexual touching from a person with a mental disability within section 376F(1)` f IF
        "(a) A intentionally touches another person (B) or intentionally incites B to touch A or B or another person"
   ...    (f's `A intentionally touches B` OR f's `A intentionally incites B to touch A or B or another person`)
   ...  "(b) the touching is sexual and B consents to the touching"
   ...  (f's `the touching is sexual` AND f's `B consents to the touching`)
   ...  "(c) A obtains B's consent (i) where B is not A's spouse, by means of an inducement offered or given, a threat made or a deception practised by A for that purpose; or (ii) where B is A's spouse, by means of a threat made or a deception practised by A for that purpose"
   ...    ((f's `B is not A's spouse` AND (f's `A obtains B's consent by means of an inducement offered or given by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a threat made by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a deception practised by A for that purpose`)) OR (f's `B is A's spouse` AND (f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a threat made by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a deception practised by A for that purpose`)))
   ...  "(ca) B has a mental disability; and (d) A knows or could reasonably be expected to know that B has a mental disability"
   ...  (f's `B has a mental disability within section 376F(5)` AND f's `A knows or could reasonably be expected to know that B has a mental disability`)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F(2) (src:8822-8824)
`punishment prescribed by s 376F(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376F(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `or with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F(2) (src:8822-8824)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376F(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (procuring sexual activity with a person with a mental disability, no penetration)
GIVEN f IS A `Mental Disability Procurement Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376F(2)` f IF
        "Subject to subsection (3), a person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments"
   ...  `procures sexual touching from a person with a mental disability within section 376F(1)` f AND NOT (f's `the touching involved penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis`)

GIVEN f IS A `Mental Disability Procurement Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of procurement of sexual activity with person with mental disability not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally touches B` OR f's `A intentionally incites B to touch A or B or another person`) "A intentionally touches B or intentionally incites B to touch A or B or another person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the touching is sexual` AND f's `B consents to the touching`) "the touching is sexual and B consents to it"),
        (`missing unless` ((f's `B is not A's spouse` AND (f's `A obtains B's consent by means of an inducement offered or given by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a threat made by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a deception practised by A for that purpose`)) OR (f's `B is A's spouse` AND (f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a threat made by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a deception practised by A for that purpose`))) "A obtains B's consent by inducement, threat or deception where B is not A's spouse, or by threat or deception where B is A's spouse"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B has a mental disability within section 376F(5)` AND f's `A knows or could reasonably be expected to know that B has a mental disability`) "B has a mental disability and A knows or could reasonably be expected to know it"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `the touching involved penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis`)) "the touching did not involve penetration (otherwise section 376F(3) applies)"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376F(2)` f) "the elements of section 376F(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F(2) (src:8822-8824)
@export Frame a charge under section 376F(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (procuring sexual activity with a person with a mental disability, no penetration), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mental Disability Procurement Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376F(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376F(2)" "procurement of sexual activity with person with mental disability"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376F(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376F(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally touch, or incite to touch, ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person with a mental disability, in a sexual touching to which the said person consented because you obtained the consent by inducement, threat or deception, knowing or being reasonably expected to know that the said person had a mental disability, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of procurement of sexual activity with person with mental disability not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F(3) (src:8835-8837)
`punishment prescribed by s 376F(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376F(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to a fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F(3) (src:8835-8837)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376F(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (procuring sexual activity with a person with a mental disability, with penetration)
GIVEN f IS A `Mental Disability Procurement Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376F(3)` f IF
        "a person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to a fine or to caning"
   ...  `procures sexual touching from a person with a mental disability within section 376F(1)` f AND f's `the touching involved penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis`

GIVEN f IS A `Mental Disability Procurement Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of procurement of sexual activity with person with mental disability involving penetration not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally touches B` OR f's `A intentionally incites B to touch A or B or another person`) "A intentionally touches B or intentionally incites B to touch A or B or another person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the touching is sexual` AND f's `B consents to the touching`) "the touching is sexual and B consents to it"),
        (`missing unless` ((f's `B is not A's spouse` AND (f's `A obtains B's consent by means of an inducement offered or given by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a threat made by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a deception practised by A for that purpose`)) OR (f's `B is A's spouse` AND (f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a threat made by A for that purpose` OR f's `A obtains B's consent by means of a deception practised by A for that purpose`))) "A obtains B's consent by inducement, threat or deception where B is not A's spouse, or by threat or deception where B is A's spouse"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B has a mental disability within section 376F(5)` AND f's `A knows or could reasonably be expected to know that B has a mental disability`) "B has a mental disability and A knows or could reasonably be expected to know it"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the touching involved penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis`) "the touching involved penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376F(3)` f) "the elements of section 376F(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F(3) (src:8835-8837)
@export Frame a charge under section 376F(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (procuring sexual activity with a person with a mental disability, with penetration), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mental Disability Procurement Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376F(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376F(3)" "procurement of sexual activity with person with mental disability involving penetration"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376F(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376F(3)` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally touch, or incite to touch, ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a person with a mental disability, in a sexual touching involving penetration to which the said person consented because you obtained the consent by inducement, threat or deception, knowing or being reasonably expected to know that the said person had a mental disability, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of procurement of sexual activity with person with mental disability involving penetration not made out` f)

-- 376F(5): "mental disability" means ...
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376F(5) (src:8843-8846)
@export Whether an impairment is a "mental disability" within section 376F(5) of the Penal Code 1871: an impairment of or disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain, resulting from any disability or disorder of the mind or brain, which impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the giving of consent to sexual touching
GIVEN `there is an impairment of or a disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain resulting from a disability or disorder of the mind or brain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such an impairment or disturbance?
      `it impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the giving of consent to sexual touching` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it impair that ability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376F(5) the impairment is a mental disability` MEANS
    IF `there is an impairment of or a disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain resulting from a disability or disorder of the mind or brain`
        AND `it impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the giving of consent to sexual touching`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"mental disability\" means an impairment of or a disturbance in the functioning of the mind or brain ... which impairs the ability to make a proper judgement in the giving of consent to sexual touching"



§§ `s 376G - incest`

-- src:8850 | Incest
-- src:8852 | 376G.—(1) Any person (A) of or above 16 years of age who —
-- src:8854 | (a) penetrates, with A’s penis, the vagina, anus or mouth, as the case may be,
-- src:8855 | of a person of or above 16 years of age who is a close family relative (B);
-- src:8857 | (b) sexually penetrates, with a part of A’s body (other than A’s penis, if A is a
-- src:8858 | man) or anything else, the vagina or anus, as the case may be, of a person
-- src:8861 | of or above 16 years of age who is a close family relative (B);
-- src:8863 | (c) causes or permits a man of or above 16 years of age who is a close family
-- src:8864 | relative (B) to penetrate, with B’s penis, the vagina, anus or mouth, as the
-- src:8865 | case may be, of A; or
-- src:8867 | (d) causes or permits a person of or above 16 years of age who is a close
-- src:8868 | family relative (B) to sexually penetrate, with a part of B’s body (other
-- src:8869 | than B’s penis, if B is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus, as the
-- src:8870 | case may be, of A,
-- src:8872 | knowing that B is a close family relative, shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:8876 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), B is a close family relative of A if B is A’s
-- src:8877 | grandchild, child, sibling, half-sibling, parent or grandparent (whether such relationship
-- src:8878 | is or is not traced through lawful wedlock).
-- src:8882 | (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with
-- src:8883 | imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years.
-- src:8887 | (4) This section does not apply to an act of penetration mentioned in subsection (1)
-- src:8888 | which would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or
-- src:8889 | 376AA(1).
-- src:8894 | (5) To avoid doubt —
-- src:8896 | (a) it is not necessary for the prosecution to prove that B did consent to the act
-- src:8897 | of penetration mentioned in subsection (1); and
-- src:8899 | (b) it is not a defence that B did consent to that act.
-- src:8903 | (6) A person below 18 years of age who is a victim of an offence under
-- src:8904 | section 376AA is not guilty of an offence under this section in respect of the same acts
-- src:8905 | constituting the offence under that section.
-- Subsection (2) defines "close family relative" ("B is a close family relative of A if ..."): `s 376G(2) B is a close family relative of A`, below.
-- Subsection (4): "an act of penetration ... which would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1)" is read over a nested
-- `Sexual Penetration Facts` for the same act, which the caller supplies (FORK DEF-B6). Subsection (5), consent immaterial, is `s 376G(5)` below.
-- Subsection (6) is read as a flat negative applying to the whole offence (marginal reading a).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G (src:8850-8905)
DECLARE `Incest Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the close family relative (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by having sexual intercourse with the said B, A's sister"
    `A is of or above 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused (A) of or above 16 years of age? Set from NOT `below 16 years of age` on A's age
    `A penetrates, with A's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A penetrate, with A's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of B? (s 376G(1)(a))
    `A sexually penetrates, with a part of A's body (other than A's penis, if A is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A sexually penetrate, with a part of A's body (other than A's penis, if A is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of B? (s 376G(1)(b))
    `A causes or permits B, a man, to penetrate, with B's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A cause or permit B, a man, to penetrate, with B's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of A? (s 376G(1)(c))
    `A causes or permits B to sexually penetrate, with a part of B's body (other than B's penis, if B is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A cause or permit B to sexually penetrate, with a part of B's body (other than B's penis, if B is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of A? (s 376G(1)(d))
    `B is of or above 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B of or above 16 years of age? Set from NOT `below 16 years of age` on B's age (s 376G(1)(a)-(d))
    `B is a close family relative of A within section 376G(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B a close family relative of A - A's grandchild, child, sibling, half-sibling, parent or grandparent, whether or not the relationship is traced through lawful wedlock (s 376G(2))? Set from `s 376G(2) B is a close family relative of A`
    `A knows that B is a close family relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know that B is a close family relative? (s 376G(1))
    `the act of penetration, as the facts of an offence under sections 375, 376 or 376AA` IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The facts of the same act of penetration, read under ss 375, 376 and 376AA. If they make out an offence under s 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1), s 376G does not apply (s 376G(4))
    `A is below 18 years of age and is a victim of an offence under section 376AA in respect of the same acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is A below 18 years of age and a victim of an offence under s 376AA in respect of the same acts? (s 376G(6): then A is not guilty under this section)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G (src:8852-8872)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376G(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (incest: sexual penetration with a close family relative of or above 16 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Incest Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has sexual penetration with a close family relative within section 376G(1)` f IF
        f's `A is of or above 16 years of age`
   ...  "(a)-(d) penetrates, sexually penetrates, causes or permits penetration of or by a person of or above 16 years of age who is a close family relative (B)"
   ...  ((f's `A penetrates, with A's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of B` OR f's `A sexually penetrates, with a part of A's body (other than A's penis, if A is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of B` OR f's `A causes or permits B, a man, to penetrate, with B's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of A` OR f's `A causes or permits B to sexually penetrate, with a part of B's body (other than B's penis, if B is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of A`) AND f's `B is of or above 16 years of age` AND f's `B is a close family relative of A within section 376G(2)`)
   ...  "knowing that B is a close family relative"
   ...  f's `A knows that B is a close family relative`
   ...  "(4) This section does not apply to an act of penetration mentioned in subsection (1) which would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1)"
   ...  (NOT (`an act of penetration excluded from section 376G by section 376G(4)` (f's `the act of penetration, as the facts of an offence under sections 375, 376 or 376AA`)))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to an act of penetration mentioned in subsection (1) which would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1)"
   ...  "(6) A person below 18 years of age who is a victim of an offence under section 376AA is not guilty of an offence under this section in respect of the same acts constituting the offence under that section"
   ...  (NOT (f's `A is below 18 years of age and is a victim of an offence under section 376AA in respect of the same acts`))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not guilty of an offence under this section in respect of the same acts constituting the offence under that section"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(3) (src:8882-8883)
`punishment prescribed by s 376G(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376G(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(3) (src:8882-8883)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376G(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (incest)
GIVEN f IS A `Incest Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376G(3)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years"
   ...  `has sexual penetration with a close family relative within section 376G(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Incest Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of incest not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A is of or above 16 years of age`) "A is of or above 16 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` ((f's `A penetrates, with A's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of B` OR f's `A sexually penetrates, with a part of A's body (other than A's penis, if A is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of B` OR f's `A causes or permits B, a man, to penetrate, with B's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of A` OR f's `A causes or permits B to sexually penetrate, with a part of B's body (other than B's penis, if B is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of A`) AND f's `B is of or above 16 years of age` AND f's `B is a close family relative of A within section 376G(2)`) "A penetrates, or causes or permits penetration with, a close family relative B of or above 16 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knows that B is a close family relative`) "A knows that B is a close family relative"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (`an act of penetration excluded from section 376G by section 376G(4)` (f's `the act of penetration, as the facts of an offence under sections 375, 376 or 376AA`))) "the act would not constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1) (section 376G(4))"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `A is below 18 years of age and is a victim of an offence under section 376AA in respect of the same acts`)) "A is not a person below 18 years of age who is a victim of an offence under section 376AA in respect of the same acts (section 376G(6))"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376G(3)` f) "the elements of section 376G(3) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(3) (src:8882-8883)
@export Frame a charge under section 376G(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (incest), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Incest Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376G(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376G(3)" "incest"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376G(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376G(3)` f)
        (CONCAT "being of or above 16 years of age, did have sexual penetration with ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a close family relative of or above 16 years of age, knowing that the said person was a close family relative, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of incest not made out` f)

-- 376G(2): "B is a close family relative of A if B is A's grandchild, child, sibling, half-sibling, parent or grandparent"
DECLARE `Relation of B to A` IS ONE OF
    grandchild
    child
    sibling
    `half-sibling`
    parent
    grandparent
    `another relation`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(2) (src:8876-8878)
@export Whether B is a "close family relative" of A within section 376G(2) of the Penal Code 1871, by B's relation to A (whether or not the relationship is traced through lawful wedlock)
GIVEN relation IS A `Relation of B to A` @desc B's relation to A
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376G(2) B is a close family relative of A` MEANS
    CONSIDER relation
    WHEN grandchild THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN child THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN sibling THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `half-sibling` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN parent THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN grandparent THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another relation` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "B is a close family relative of A if B is A's grandchild, child, sibling, half-sibling, parent or grandparent" (an "if" read as closing the list: marginal reading a)

-- 376G(4): the act that "would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1)"
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(4) (src:8887-8889)
@export Whether an act of penetration is one that would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1) of the Penal Code 1871, so that section 376G does not apply to it
GIVEN n IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The facts of the same act of penetration, read under sections 375, 376 and 376AA
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an act of penetration excluded from section 376G by section 376G(4)` n IF
        (        n's `the accused is a man`
            AND  n's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis`
            AND  n's `the victim is a woman`
            AND  `without consent within section 375(a)` n )
    OR  (        n's `the accused is a man`
            AND  n's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis`
            AND  `without consent within section 375(a)` n )
    OR  `commits sexual assault by penetration within section 376(2)` n
    OR  `commits exploitative sexual penetration of a minor within section 376AA(1)` n

-- 376G(5) and 376A(1B): consent is immaterial ("To avoid doubt")
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(5) (src:8894-8899)
@export Whether, under section 376G(5)(a) of the Penal Code 1871, the prosecution must prove that B did consent to the act of penetration: it need not
GIVEN `B did consent to the act of penetration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B consent? The answer changes nothing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376G(5)(a) the prosecution must prove that B did consent` MEANS
    JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecution to prove that B did consent to the act of penetration"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376G(5) (src:8894-8899)
@export Whether, under section 376G(5)(b) of the Penal Code 1871, it is a defence that B did consent to the act of penetration: it is not
GIVEN `B did consent to the act of penetration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B consent? The answer changes nothing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376G(5)(b) B's consent is a defence` MEANS
    JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not a defence that B did consent to that act"



§§ `s 376H - procurement of sexual activity by deception or false representation`

-- src:8909 | Procurement of sexual activity by deception or false representation
-- src:8910 | 376H.—(1) Any person (A) shall be guilty of an offence if —
-- src:8911 | (a) A intentionally touches another person (B) or intentionally incites B to —
-- src:8912 | (i) touch A or the bodily fluids of A;
-- src:8915 | (ii) touch B;
-- src:8917 | (iii) touch another person (C) or the bodily fluids of C; or
-- src:8919 | (iv) be touched by C;
-- src:8923 | (b) the touching is sexual and B consents to the touching;
-- src:8925 | (c) A fraudulently obtains B’s consent by means of deception or false
-- src:8926 | representation practised or made by A for that purpose;
-- src:8928 | (d) the deception or false representation mentioned in paragraph (c) relates
-- src:8929 | to —
-- src:8930 | (i) the use or manner of use of any sexually protective measure; or
-- src:8932 | (ii) the risk of B contracting a sexually transmitted disease from the
-- src:8933 | touching; and
-- src:8937 | (e) A knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in
-- src:8938 | consequence of such deception or false representation.
-- src:8942 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall —
-- src:8944 | (a) in the case where the sexual touching mentioned in that subsection
-- src:8945 | involved —
-- src:8947 | (i) penetration of the vagina or anus (as the case may be) with a
-- src:8948 | part of the body or anything else; or
-- src:8950 | (ii) penetration of the mouth with the penis,
-- src:8951 | be punished on conviction with imprisonment for a term which may
-- src:8952 | extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with caning, or any combination of
-- src:8953 | such punishments; and
-- src:8955 | (b) in any other case, be punished on conviction with imprisonment for a term
-- src:8956 | which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- src:8960 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1) —
-- src:8962 | (a) a person makes a false representation if it is untrue or misleading, and that
-- src:8963 | person knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading;
-- src:8965 | (b) a representation may be express or implied; and
-- src:8968 | (c) a “sexually protective measure” means —
-- src:8969 | (i) where B is female, a device, drug or medical procedure to
-- src:8970 | prevent pregnancy or sexually transmitted diseases as a result of
-- src:8971 | sexual intercourse; or
-- src:8973 | (ii) where B is male, a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent
-- src:8974 | sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse.
-- Subsection (3) gives three rules of reading - a false representation, express or implied, "sexually protective measure" - each a function below.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H (src:8909-8974)
DECLARE `Deceptive Procurement Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person touched (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by falsely telling the said person that a condom was being worn"
    `A intentionally touches B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally touch B? (s 376H(1)(a))
    `A intentionally incites B to touch A or the bodily fluids of A, to touch B, to touch another person (C) or the bodily fluids of C, or to be touched by C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A intentionally incite B to touch A or the bodily fluids of A, to touch B, to touch another person (C) or the bodily fluids of C, or to be touched by C? (s 376H(1)(a)(i)-(iv))
    `the touching is sexual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the touching sexual - as s 377C(3)(d) says? (s 376H(1)(b)) See `s 377C(3)(d) the conduct is sexual`
    `B consents to the touching` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B consent to the touching? (s 376H(1)(b))
    `A fraudulently obtains B's consent by means of deception or false representation practised or made by A for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A fraudulently obtain B's consent by means of a deception or false representation practised or made by A for that purpose? A false representation is read with `s 376H(3)(a) the representation is false` and `s 376H(3)(b) the representation is express or implied` (s 376H(1)(c))
    `the deception or false representation relates to the use or manner of use of any sexually protective measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the deception or false representation relate to the use or manner of use of any sexually protective measure? (s 376H(1)(d)(i)) See `s 376H(3)(c) the thing is a sexually protective measure`
    `the deception or false representation relates to the risk of B contracting a sexually transmitted disease from the touching` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the deception or false representation relate to the risk of B contracting a sexually transmitted disease from the touching? (s 376H(1)(d)(ii))
    `A knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of such deception or false representation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A know, or have reason to believe, that the consent was given in consequence of such deception or false representation? (s 376H(1)(e))
    `the touching involved penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sexual touching involve penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 376H(2) states (10 years, or 2 years)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H (src:8910-8938)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 376H(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (procuring a sexual touching by deception or false representation about a sexually protective measure or the risk of a sexually transmitted disease)
GIVEN f IS A `Deceptive Procurement Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `procures sexual touching by deception or false representation within section 376H(1)` f IF
        "(a) A intentionally touches another person (B) or intentionally incites B to (i) touch A or the bodily fluids of A; (ii) touch B; (iii) touch another person (C) or the bodily fluids of C; or (iv) be touched by C"
   ...    (f's `A intentionally touches B` OR f's `A intentionally incites B to touch A or the bodily fluids of A, to touch B, to touch another person (C) or the bodily fluids of C, or to be touched by C`)
   ...  "(b) the touching is sexual and B consents to the touching"
   ...  (f's `the touching is sexual` AND f's `B consents to the touching`)
   ...  "(c) A fraudulently obtains B's consent by means of deception or false representation practised or made by A for that purpose"
   ...  f's `A fraudulently obtains B's consent by means of deception or false representation practised or made by A for that purpose`
   ...  "(d) the deception or false representation relates to (i) the use or manner of use of any sexually protective measure; or (ii) the risk of B contracting a sexually transmitted disease from the touching"
   ...    (f's `the deception or false representation relates to the use or manner of use of any sexually protective measure` OR f's `the deception or false representation relates to the risk of B contracting a sexually transmitted disease from the touching`)
   ...  "(e) A knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of such deception or false representation"
   ...  f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of such deception or false representation`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(2)(a) (src:8942-8953)
`punishment prescribed by s 376H(2)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376H(2)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with caning, or any combination of such punishments"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `or with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(2)(b) (src:8955-8956)
`punishment prescribed by s 376H(2)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376H(2)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(2) (src:8942-8956)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376H(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (procuring sexual activity by deception or false representation)
GIVEN f IS A `Deceptive Procurement Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376H(2)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall be punished"
   ...  `procures sexual touching by deception or false representation within section 376H(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Deceptive Procurement Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of procurement of sexual activity by deception or false representation not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `A intentionally touches B` OR f's `A intentionally incites B to touch A or the bodily fluids of A, to touch B, to touch another person (C) or the bodily fluids of C, or to be touched by C`) "A intentionally touches B or intentionally incites B to touch or be touched"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the touching is sexual` AND f's `B consents to the touching`) "the touching is sexual and B consents to it"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A fraudulently obtains B's consent by means of deception or false representation practised or made by A for that purpose`) "A fraudulently obtains B's consent by deception or false representation"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the deception or false representation relates to the use or manner of use of any sexually protective measure` OR f's `the deception or false representation relates to the risk of B contracting a sexually transmitted disease from the touching`) "the deception or false representation relates to the use or manner of use of a sexually protective measure, or to the risk of B contracting a sexually transmitted disease"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of such deception or false representation`) "A knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of the deception or false representation"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 376H(2)` f) "the elements of section 376H(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(2) (src:8942-8956)
@export Frame a charge under section 376H(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (procuring sexual activity by deception or false representation), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Deceptive Procurement Facts` @desc The facts of the case and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376H(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376H(2)" "procurement of sexual activity by deception or false representation"
        (IF f's `the touching involved penetration of the vagina or anus with a part of the body or anything else, or penetration of the mouth with the penis` THEN `punishment prescribed by s 376H(2)(a)`'s words ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 376H(2)(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376H(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally touch, or incite to touch, ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), " in a sexual touching to which the said person consented, having fraudulently obtained the consent by a deception or false representation relating to a sexually protective measure or to the risk of contracting a sexually transmitted disease, knowing or having reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of it, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of procurement of sexual activity by deception or false representation not made out` f)

-- 376H(3): rules of reading
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(3)(a) (src:8962-8963)
@export Whether a person makes a "false representation" within section 376H(3)(a) of the Penal Code 1871: the representation is untrue or misleading, and the person knows that it is, or might be
GIVEN `the representation is untrue or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the representation untrue or misleading?
      `the person knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person who made it know that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376H(3)(a) the representation is false` MEANS
    IF `the representation is untrue or misleading` AND `the person knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person makes a false representation if it is untrue or misleading, and that person knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading" (an "if" read as closed: marginal reading a)

DECLARE `Form of a representation` IS ONE OF
    express
    implied
    `some other form of representation`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(3)(b) (src:8965-8965)
@export Whether a representation of the given form is a representation within section 376H(3)(b) of the Penal Code 1871: "a representation may be express or implied"
GIVEN form IS A `Form of a representation` @desc The form in which the representation was made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376H(3)(b) the representation is express or implied` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN express THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN implied THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `some other form of representation` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a representation may be express or implied" says two forms count; it does not say that a representation in no such form is not one

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376H(3)(c) (src:8968-8974)
@export Whether a thing is a "sexually protective measure" within section 376H(3)(c) of the Penal Code 1871: where B is female, a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent pregnancy or sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse; where B is male, one to prevent sexually transmitted diseases
GIVEN `B is female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B female?
      `B is male` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B male?
      `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent pregnancy as a result of sexual intercourse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent pregnancy as a result of sexual intercourse?
      `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376H(3)(c) the thing is a sexually protective measure` MEANS
    IF (        `B is female`
           AND  (     `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent pregnancy as a result of sexual intercourse`
                  OR  `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse` ) )
       OR  (    `B is male`
           AND  `it is a device, drug or medical procedure to prevent sexually transmitted diseases as a result of sexual intercourse` )
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a \"sexually protective measure\" means ..." (a closed definition)



§§ `s 377 - sexual penetration, etc., of a corpse`

-- src:8978 | Sexual penetration, etc., of a corpse
-- src:8980 | 377.—(1) A person (A) who —
-- src:8982 | (a) penetrates, with A’s penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of a human corpse;
-- src:8984 | (b) sexually penetrates, with a part of A’s body (other than A’s penis, if A is a
-- src:8985 | man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of a human corpse;
-- src:8987 | (c) causes A’s vagina, anus or mouth to be penetrated by the penis of a human
-- src:8988 | corpse;
-- src:8990 | (d) causes A’s vagina or anus to be sexually penetrated by a part of a human
-- src:8991 | corpse (other than the penis, if the human corpse is that of a deceased
-- src:8992 | man);
-- src:8994 | (e) causes a person (B) to penetrate, with B’s penis (if B is a man), the vagina,
-- src:8995 | anus or mouth of a human corpse, without B’s consent;
-- src:8997 | (f) causes B to sexually penetrate, with a part of B’s body (other than B’s
-- src:8998 | penis, if B is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of a human
-- src:8999 | corpse, without B’s consent;
-- src:9001 | (g) causes B’s vagina, anus or mouth to be penetrated by the penis of a human
-- src:9002 | corpse, without B’s consent; or
-- src:9004 | (h) causes B’s vagina or anus to be sexually penetrated by a part of a human
-- src:9005 | corpse (other than the penis, if the human corpse is that of a deceased
-- src:9006 | man), without B’s consent,
-- src:9008 | shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:9010 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) shall
-- src:9011 | be punished with imprisonment for a term that may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or
-- src:9012 | with both.
-- src:9014 | (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)(e), (f), (g) or (h) shall
-- src:9017 | be punished with imprisonment for a term that may extend to 20 years, and shall also be
-- src:9018 | liable to fine or to caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377 (src:8978-9018)
DECLARE `Corpse Penetration Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc A description of the corpse, or the name of the person (B) caused to penetrate or be penetrated, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by penetrating the vagina of the body of the late Tan Mei Ling with your penis"
    `A penetrates, with A's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth of a human corpse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do this? (s 377(1)(a))
    `A sexually penetrates, with a part of A's body (other than A's penis, if A is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of a human corpse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do this? (s 377(1)(b))
    `A causes A's vagina, anus or mouth to be penetrated by the penis of a human corpse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do this? (s 377(1)(c))
    `A causes A's vagina or anus to be sexually penetrated by a part of a human corpse (other than the penis, if the human corpse is that of a deceased man)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do this? (s 377(1)(d))
    `A causes a person (B) to penetrate, with B's penis (if B is a man), the vagina, anus or mouth of a human corpse, without B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do this, B not consenting? (s 377(1)(e))
    `A causes B to sexually penetrate, with a part of B's body (other than B's penis, if B is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus of a human corpse, without B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do this, B not consenting? (s 377(1)(f))
    `A causes B's vagina, anus or mouth to be penetrated by the penis of a human corpse, without B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do this, B not consenting? (s 377(1)(g))
    `A causes B's vagina or anus to be sexually penetrated by a part of a human corpse (other than the penis, if the human corpse is that of a deceased man), without B's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A do this, B not consenting? (s 377(1)(h))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377 (src:8980-8992)
